hadiths[683]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was asked about such water that is in a desert and in which beasts and animals come to drink, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""When the water is clean, nothing defiles it."" One tradition has these words: ""He is not defiled."" There are similar words in a tradition."
"2","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about water from which animals and beasts come to drink, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the water is two-fold"
"3","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates to his father, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink, so he said: \When the water is two cups"
"4","This tradition is narrated from some other traditions."
"5","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the following statement from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar radi Allahu anhuma): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a water from which animals and beasts drink. One tradition has these words: beasts and beasts. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water is two-fold"
"6","The same hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: animals and beasts (meaning the word animal is transmitted first)."
"7","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When the water is two cups, it is not najis (the narrator doubts that perhaps these words are: not impure)."""
"8","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When water is divided into two parts"
"9","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"10","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"11","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"12","Narrated by Abdullah bin Umar: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"
"13","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the same from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abdullah, his father (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"15","Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two cups"
"16","Ubaidullah narrates this on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, being asked about water that is in a deserted place and animals and beasts drink from it, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""When the water becomes two folds, it is not impure."" A narrator named Ibn Arfa narrates: I heard a narrator named Hashim explaining ""Qala"" and he says: It means two large pots."
"17","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I heard the Holy Prophet (PBUH) saying this: A person asked him about such water, which is in a deserted place, from which animals and beasts drink, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When the water is divided"
"18","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"19","The same tradition is narrated from another hadith."
"20","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He was asked about a well into which dead bodies are put, and from which dogs and other animals drink water. The same hadith is narrated on the authority of Ubaidullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission."
"21","The same hadith along with some other traditions is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar). However, some narrators have also quoted it as a \suspended\"" tradition."""""
"22","Asim bin Munzar narrates: I entered a garden with Ubaidullah bin Abdullah, in which there was a pool of water with the skin of a dead camel lying on it, so Ubaydullah bin Abdullah performed ablution on it. The skin of a dead camel is lying inside it, so he told me this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father."
"23","This hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but in this chain of transmission, the words ""the narrator is in doubt, or perhaps three forts"" are not recorded in this chain of transmission. The same tradition is also narrated by another person in which these words are: ""When the water becomes two forts, (the narrator doubts) perhaps these words will become three forts."" That's it."
"24","Abd al-Jabar al-Makki and Musa ibn Ismail and Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Aishah narrated this chain of narration on the authority of Hamad ibn Salama and they said in it: If the water is two qala, it is not najis. They did not say \or three\""."""""
"25","Asim bin Munzar narrates: We were in a garden. The narrator has doubts. These words are: He was ours or perhaps these words were Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abdullah's. Meanwhile, when it was time for prayer, Abdullah got up, and went to the tank in the garden and started performing ablution from it. Although the skin of a camel was lying in this tank, I said: You are performing ablution with it, if it has skin. He said: My father narrated this hadith to me regarding the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two cups"
"26","The judge Al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us. And Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Shīrāzī narrated to us; they both said: Al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; he said: Bishr ibn al-Sarī and Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir, with this chain of transmission, similar to the statement of ʿAffān: ""When the water amounts to two qullahs, it does not become impure."""""
"27","The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, which has these words: \When water becomes two-fold"
"28","Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"
"29","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""When the water becomes two-fold, nothing impures it."" In some hadiths, these words are transmitted as ""marfu'"" hadith, while in others, they are transmitted as ""mawfuk"" hadith."
"30","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is related to Mujahid from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (Radi Allahu Anhu) as a “Mowquf” Hadith."
"31","Asim says: The word \al-Qalal\"" used in the text of hadiths refers to \""big pots\""."""""
"32","Yahya bin Aqeel narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""When water becomes two-fold, it is not impure and there is no harm (in using it)."" The narrator narrates: I inquired from my teacher Yahya bin Aqeel, what is meant by ""Hijr""? So they replied: It means the matka of Hijr, so I guessed: one qala is equal to two ""farq"". Mujahid narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: ""When the water is two qalas or more, nothing impures it."""
"33","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When I was raised from the seventh heaven towards the Sadrat al-Muntahi, its fruits were as large as the fruits of the Hijr, and its leaves were like the ears of an elephant. What is it? So they said: The inner rivers are in Paradise and the outer rivers are the Nile and the Euphrates.\""34"""""
"34","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Salih al-Kufi narrated to us: ‘Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Baladi narrated to us: Isma‘il ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn ‘Ulwan narrated to us from Nafi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out on one of his journeys and traveled by night. They passed by a man sitting by his watering trough. ‘Umar said: “O owner of the trough, did wild beasts drink from your trough tonight?” The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “O owner of the trough, do not inform him; this is a drinking place for them. They have what they carried in their bellies, and for us remains a drink that is pure and purifying.”"
"35","This hadith is also narrated along with another document."
"36","Wakiyya says: The learned note everything, whether it is in their favor or not, and the heretics only note that which is in their favor."
"37","Yahya bin Abu Zaida says: It is better to note the hadith than not to note it."
"38","Sayyiduna Jabir Ibn Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the water reaches the limit of forty Qala, it is not impure."" The same hadith is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission, but there is an illusion in its chain of transmission. Another narrator has narrated this tradition as a ""Muquf"" tradition from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission. The same tradition is narrated from Ibn Mankadir as his own saying along with another chain of transmission, which reads: ""Do not exceed this."""
"39","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the water becomes 40 galahs"
"40","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) says: ""When the water is forty qala, then nothing impures it."""
"41","This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA)."
"42","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: ""When the water becomes forty qala, then nothing impures it."""
"43","Muhammad bin Mankader narrates: When the water is 40 feet deep, it is not impure, or perhaps a word similar to this has been described by him."
"44","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Hurairah narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him), he says: ""When the water reaches the amount of forty Qala, it is not impure."" This tradition has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (Radi Allahu Anhu) along with some other traditions. In some traditions, the word ""forty large buckets"" has been used, in some traditions, the word ""forty small buckets"" has been used (that is, this word has been used instead of ""Qala"")."
"45","Sayyiduna Thawban Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Water is a purifying thing, except for that water whose smell or taste (impure thing) prevails."""
"46","Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Nothing defiles water, except that which changes its taste or smell."" The above-mentioned hadith is transmitted to Rashid bin Saad, however, Azizi has quoted this hadith on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Maama."
"47","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Nothing defiles water, except that which changes the smell and taste of that water."" This hadith has been quoted as ""marfu'"" only from Rashid bin Sa'd and this narrator is not authentic, it is Sahih, it is narrated on the authority of Rashid bin Sa'd."
"48","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Nothing defiles water.\"""""""
"49","Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Nothing defiles water except that which overpowers its smell or taste.\"" This hadith is \""musal\"" and a narrator named Abu Usama transmitted it to Rashid bin Sa'd as a \""mawquf\"" hadith."""""
"50","Abu Awun Rashid bin Sa'd states: Nothing defiles water, except that which changes the smell or taste of the water."
"51","Saeed bin Musayyib says: Water is pure, nothing impures it."
"52","Dawood bin Abu Hind narrates: We asked Saeed bin Musaib about a well and a reservoir from which even dogs drink, so he said: Water has been revealed as a pure thing, nothing defiles it."
"53","Dawood quotes the statement of Saeed bin Musaib: \Allah has revealed water as a pure thing"
"54","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution from the ""Baa'a"" well, although menstruating women's clothes and other dirty things are put into it. One tradition has these words: ""Dead"" is thrown. Some narrators have quoted these words: Dog meat is put. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Water is pure, nothing impures it."" These words of the hadith are in accordance with the words narrated by the narrator named Ibn Abu Aoun."
"55","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: I heard from the Prophet (PBUH), when he was asked: O Messenger of Allah! We drink water from the well of ""Baa'ah"", although the meat of dogs, the clothes of menstruating women and the filth of people are put into it (so what is the ruling on this)? The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Water is pure, nothing impures it."" This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but there is some difference in its chain of transmission."
"56","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about these reservoirs, which come at different places on the way to Makkah and Medina. He was told: Dogs and beasts drink water from these reservoirs. The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whatever they put in their stomachs is their air"
"57","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): Water is brought for you from a well called ""Baa'ah"", which is the well of Banu Sa'idah. In this well, the clothes of menstruating women, the meat of dogs and the filth of people are put. She doesn't."""
"58","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
"59","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution from a well called Baa'a? In which the clothes of menstruating women, the meat of dogs and dirt are put, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Water is pure and nothing impures it.\"""""""
"60","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA)."
"61","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) drank the water of the \Baa'a\"" well."""""
"62","Abu Sa'eed and Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrate: Once Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Amr ibn al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, passed by a reservoir, and Sayyidna Amr, may God be pleased with him, inquired: O owner of the tank! Do the beasts also come and drink water at this reservoir of yours? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: \O owner of the reservoir! Do not tell us about this (because to drink water from such a reservoir) sometimes we come after the beasts and sometimes they come after us.\"""""""
"63","Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: When we were in Syria, I brought water to the service of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, he performed ablution with this water and then inquired: Where did you bring this water from? I have never seen any heavenly water sweeter and purer than this. Narrator narrates: I said: I have brought it from the house of an old Christian woman. When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) performed ablution, he came to her. He said: ""O old woman! Accept Islam, you will be safe. Allah Almighty has sent Sayyiduna Muhammad (PBUH) with the truth."" Narrator narrates: This woman removed the veil from her head and her hair was white like flowers. The old woman said: Now I am about to die, then Sayyiduna Umar said: ""O Allah! Be a witness!"""
"64","Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: Sayyiduna Umar performed ablution at the house of a Christian, then he went to this woman, he said: ""O big sister! Accept Islam, you will be safe. Allah Almighty has sent Sayyidna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the truth."" When this woman removed the veil from her head, (her hair was white like a flower), this old woman said: Now I am about to die. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: ""O Allah! Be a witness."""
"65","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: Once an Abyssinian fell into the well of Zamzam, i.e. he fell down and died, his body was taken out under the order of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) and about the well, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) instructed that it be cleaned. The narrator narrates: But the water of the spring did not come under the control of the people, it came from the rock (black stone). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) instructed about it: It should be completely covered with cloths, until it is completely covered, when people closed it, then water came out of it."
"66","Sayyiduna Abu Tufail narrates: Once a boy fell into the well of Zam Zam and all the water was taken out of him."
"67","Ibrahim Nakhai says: Every living thing whose blood is flowing (if it falls into a well), then ablution will not be performed with the water of that well. Shuba says: I think, he also mentioned the chameleon."
"68","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is purifying.\"""""""
"69","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said this about the sea: \Its water is purifying and its dead is lawful.\"""""""
"70","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the sea and he said: ""Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful."" These words of the hadith are narrated from a narrator named Fazl Bin Ziyad, in another chain of transmission this tradition is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA)."
"71","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead body is lawful.\"""""""
"72","Abu Tufail narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful.\"""""""
"73","On the authority of Imam Muhammad Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him) (Imam Zain al-Abidin may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of his father (Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him)) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the water of the sea, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.”"
"74","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""""
"75","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about sea water: \Its dead body is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""""
"76","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas."
"77","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water and he said: \Sea water is pure.\"" The narrators have narrated it in the same way"
"78","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""He who cannot be purified by the water of the sea, may Allah not purify him."" The authenticity of this hadith is ""Hasan""."
"79","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once this was mentioned to me, some people after bathing in the Sea of Khadr say: It is obligatory on us, we should also bathe with other water (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \He who is not purified by the water of the sea"
"80","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A person asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! We people travel in the sea and take a little water with us. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""""
"81","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about performing ablution with sea water, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""""
"82","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water: Should it be used for ablution? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""""
"83","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""""
"84","Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Salman! Any food or drink in which an animal (i.e. worm, spider) falls, which has no blood, and dies in the food, then it is permissible to eat and drink it, and to wash clothes and perform ablution with this water."""
"85","Aslam, a freed slave of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates: Water was heated in a pot for Sayyidna Umar (RA), and he used to bathe in it. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""""
"86","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, while I was heating some water in the sun, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O girl! Do not do this, because it may result in leprosy."" This tradition is very ""poor"", its narrator Khalid bin Ismail is ""obsolete""."
"87","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing ablution with water that has been kept in the sun, or bathing with it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \It may result in rain.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Muhammad Asim. No one else has narrated this tradition from Falih"
"88","Hasan bin Azhar narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) has said this: \Do not bathe with water heated in the sun"
"89","Hadith 85: It is narrated about Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) that: She has declared it abominable to perform ablution with water in which bread has been soaked."
"90","Zayd bin Aslam narrates: (God's guidance is:) ""When you stand for prayer, wash your faces."" Zayd bin Aslam said: It means, when you wake up from sleep."
"91","Imam Malik bin Anas has quoted Zayd bin Aslam's saying about this saying of Allah Almighty: \O you who believe! When you stand for prayer.\"" Zayd bin Aslam narrates: This means: When you wake up from sleep (do ablution)."""""
"92","Qays narrates this about Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Bijli): He used to instruct his household to perform ablution with water in which miswak was placed."
"93","Qays narrates: Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Al-Bijli, may God be pleased with him) used to instruct his family: Do ablution with the water in which I kept the miswak. Its certificate is \Correct\""."""""
"94","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to use the water left over from ablution to rub his face."
"95","Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to use the water left over from his ablution to rub his face."
"96","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever drinks something from a gold or silver vessel, or from a vessel in which gold or silver is plated, will fill his belly with Hellfire."" Its certificate is ""Hasan""."
"97","Abu Burda narrated: Once I and my father (Sayyidna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: ""The Holy Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, has forbidden to drink or eat anything in a gold or silver vessel, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, It is forbidden to use mizhah, silk cloth (there are different types of silk) and to wear gold rings.”"
"98","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he said: ""Why don't you use its skin?"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it dead? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is forbidden to eat it."" A narrator named Aqeel has added these words in his tradition: ""Can it not be purified by water and tanning."" These are the words of Ibn Hani's tradition: ""Can it not be purified by water and the bark of a betel nut?"""
"99","This tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, the narrator named Aqeel has quoted these additional words in his tradition: ""The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: Can it not be purified by tanning it with water and the bark of a cucumber?"""
"100","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he inquired: ""Whose does it belong to?"" People have said: It was given as a charity to the maidservant of Sayyida Maimunah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Why did these people not benefit from it by removing its skin and tanning it?"" People said: This is a dead body. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is forbidden to eat a dead body."""
"101","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the pet goat of one of his wives who had died. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Why don't you use its skin?"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! It is carrion, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is purified by tanning."" There is some wording difference in the tradition quoted by Ibn Sa`id (i.e. the singular pronoun is the singular masculine, instead of the feminine, the singular is absent)."
"102","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \Its meat is forbidden"
"103","This tradition is narrated from Zuhri along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Its meat has been forbidden to you and its skin (to be used) has been permitted.\"" The chain of this hadith is \""Sahih\""."""""
"104","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to the owner of a dead goat: \Why did you not skin it? You used to tan it and get profit from it.\"""""""
"105","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the pet goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Why don't you people use its skin, tan it, because in this way it becomes pure."""
"106","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \The way to purify a dead body is this: it should be tanned.\"" Ibrahim Nakhai narrates: The disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) used to say: \""The way to purify wool is this: wash it.\"""""""
"107","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: \To tan it is to purify it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""""
"108","Aaliyah bint Sabi narrates, Ms. Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told her, once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by some people of Quraish, who were pulling their sheep like a (dead) donkey is pulled. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them: \If you get his skin (it will be appropriate).\"" They said: It is dead. The Prophet"
"109","Sayyiduna Salama bin Muhibq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a woman for water, and she said: The water I have is in a bottle that belongs to a dead (animal). The woman said: Yes! The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \As a result of tanning"
"110","The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains these words: \By tanning leather"
"111","The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \It is its tanning that purifies it.\"""""""
"112","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \His tanning purifies him.\"""""""
"113","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every skin is purified by tanning.\"""""""
"114","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When the leather is tanned"
"115","We were informed by Muhammad ibn Makhlad; we were informed by Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim; Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us. And Abu Bakr al-Azraq, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Buhlul, narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ammar ibn Salam Abu Muhammad narrated to us; Zafir narrated to us; from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali; from Al-Zuhri; from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah; from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: ""Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater who eats it"" (Surah Al-An'am, verse 145). He said: ""The 'eater' (al-ta'im) is the one who eats. As for the tooth, the horn, the bone, the wool, the hair, the fur, and the sinew—there is no harm in them because they can be washed."" And Shababah said: ""Only that which is eaten of the dead animal (maytah) is forbidden, and that is the flesh. As for the skin, the tooth, the bone, the hair, and the wool—they are lawful."" Abu Bakr al-Hudhali is weak."
"116","Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates: I heard Ms. Sayyida Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrate this: She says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: ""When the skin of a dead body is tanned, then there is no harm in using it, its wool, its hair, its There is no harm in using horns, as long as they are washed with water."" The narrator of this tradition, Yusuf bin Safar, is obsolete, and no tradition other than this tradition has been narrated from him (or only he has narrated this tradition)."
"117","This tradition is narrated by Yusuf bin Safar along with another chain of transmission."
"118","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) declared the meat (eating) of a dead body to be haram, as far as its skin, hair and wool are concerned, there is nothing wrong with it. The narrator of this tradition \Abd al-Jabbar\"" is weak."""""
"119","Hazeel bin Shahrabeel narrates the following regarding Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) or Sayyida Zainab (RA) or any other wife of the Prophet (PBUH): When the goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her: ""Why don't you people use its skin?"" Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! How can we use it, it is dead, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The leather becomes pure through tanning."" The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated from a wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, whose words are: We had a goat that died."
"120","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, saying: (Allah the Exalted) said: ""Say this! In what has been revealed to me, I have not found anything that is forbidden for the one who eats it."" (The Prophet, peace be upon him, said:) ""Everything of the dead body is lawful except that which is eaten, as far as the skin, horns, hair, wool, teeth, and bones are concerned, then they are all lawful, because they are not slaughtered."" The narrator of this tradition, Abu Bakr Hazli, is ""obsolete""."
"121","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The skin that is tanned becomes pure.\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""""
"122","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Tanning the skin of a dead body purifies it.\"""""""
"123","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a goat, he inquired: ""What has happened to it?"" People said: It is dead. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""You tan its skin, because its tanning purifies it."" Qasim, the narrator of this tradition, is ""weak""."
"124","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: ""The way to purify leather is this, it should be tanned."" Its chain of transmission is ""Hasan"" and all its narrators are trustworthy."
"125","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: She had a goat which she used to milk. Once the Prophet (PBUH) did not see that goat, so he (PBUH) inquired: ""Where is the goat?"" So the people said: She is dead. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""Why don't you profit from her skin?"" We said: He is dead. The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""His tanning makes it halal, just as vinegar makes alcohol halal."" Faraj bin Fazala is unique in narrating this tradition and it is ""weak""."
"126","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""Use the skin of a dead animal, whether it has been tanned with clay, ashes, or salt, or (the narrator doubts these words:) or whatever makes it usable after (tanning)."""
"127","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand in a vessel (the narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) in the water of ablution, until he washes his hands three times, because he does not know where his hand has been throughout the night?"""
"128","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person wakes up from sleep and wants to perform ablution, he should not put his hand in the vessel until he has washed it, because he does not know where his hand has been throughout the night? And where did he keep it?"" Its certificate is ""Hasan""."
"129","Salim bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a person wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand in a vessel until he has washed it three times, because he does not know where his hand has been during the night or where his hand has circumambulated?"" A person said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: What do you think? If the person wants to perform ablution from the tank (he still has to do it)? So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar threw a pebble at him and said: ""I am narrating to you a hadith about the Holy Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, and you are saying, 'What do you think, if he had to perform ablution from a tank?'"" This tradition is authenticated by ""Hasan""."
"130","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: ""When a person wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand into a vessel until he has washed it three times, because no one knows where his hand has been throughout the night? Or where his hand has been wandering throughout the night?"" This hadith is ""Hasan""."
"131","Alqamah bin Waqqas narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, narrating this. He says: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, say: It will be counted towards the Messenger, and whoever migrated for the sake of this world in order to obtain it or migrated for a woman in order to marry her, his migration will be in the direction towards which he (intentionally) migrated.”"
"132","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, some scriptures will be brought, which will be sealed, and they will be placed before Allah, then Allah will say to His angels: Send them away! Then the angels will say: ""By Your honor! We have seen only good in them. Allah will say this, even though He has more knowledge, all these actions were for others, today I will accept only those actions, which were done only for my pleasure."
"133","Sayyidna Dahhak bin Qais Fahri (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allah Almighty says: ""I am free from partners, so whoever associates someone with Me, then that action will be for my partner (i.e., that person should seek his reward from him)."" (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Purify your actions for the sake of Allah! Because Allah will only accept the action that is pure for Him, and you should not say that it is for the sake of Allah and that is because of kinship. The reason for this is: it will be in relation to kinship, it will have nothing to do with Allah and neither will you."" Say: It is for Allah and it is because of you, because it will be because of you, it will have nothing to do with Allah."""
"134","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \No one should bathe in stagnant water when he is pregnant.\"" The narrator inquired: O Sayyidna Abu Huraira! Then what should he do? So Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""Let him get water (and bathe on one side).\"" Its certificate is \""Correct\""."""""
"135","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I remember this very well about myself and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We used to perform ablution from the same vessel."
"136","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: I remember well about myself, I used to perform ablution with the same vessel with the Holy Prophet."
"137","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of Sayyidah Maimunah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I was afflicted with janabat, I took a bath with a vessel and some water was left in it, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought Tashreef. Janabat has not been established. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a bath with this vessel. In this hadith, the narrator named Samat has been disputed and only the narrator named Sharik has stated this: It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidah Maimunah."
"138","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), men and women (i.e. husband and wife) used to perform ablution from the same vessel. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"139","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""""
"140","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (R.A.). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""""
"141","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimoona bint Harith (RA) told me this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) performed ablution with the water left over from Sayyida Maimoona’s bath. Narrator named Ramadi has narrated this: Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) performed ablution with water in the state of Janabat, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with water left over from her."
"142","Sayyidna Huqam bin Amr (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade a man to perform ablution with the water left over from a woman's ablution (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these words are:) with the water left after a woman drinks. A narrator named Shuba narrates this: Sulaiman Taymi has narrated this: Abu Hajib has narrated this with reference to a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden that a woman should perform ablution with the water left over from her ablution. The name of the narrator named Abu Hajib is Sawada bin Asim, there is a difference in this hadith regarding him, some narrators have quoted it as a “deferred” tradition as a saying of command, it has not been quoted as a “marfu’” tradition until the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him."
"143","Sayyida Khula bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: (Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) says this:) Her hand and the blessed hand of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter back and forth in the same vessel."
"144","It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him: A polytheist mocked him and said to him: I have noted this, your master has taught you everything, even the method of defecation, so Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him, replied: ""Yes! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has instructed us not to turn our backs towards the Qibla and Do not perform istujah through the right hand and do not perform istujah with less than three stones, these stones should not contain any bone or manganese.”"
"145","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"146","It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA): Some polytheists said to him: We have noted this, your master has taught you all kinds of things, even teaching you how to perform abstinence, then Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA) replied: “Yes! He should perform istanja through or facing the Qiblah, and you have also forbidden us to perform istanja with mengini and bone. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""""
"147","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said this: ""When a person goes to defecate, he should purify himself by throwing three stones. Doing so will be sufficient for him."" The authenticity of this tradition is ""Hasan""."
"148","Narrated Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to meet his needs. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) brought two stones and a ring, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the ring and said: ""This is dirt, you bring stones."" This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, according to which Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once I was going somewhere with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The narrator narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, instructed me: ""Let me bring you three stones."" The narrator narrates: I came to you with two stones and a ring, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, put the ring aside and said: ""This is dirt, you bring another thing (stone) to me instead."" In this hadith, there has been a disagreement about the narrator named Abu Ishaq, (Imam Darqutni says:) I have explained this difference at another place."
"149","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us to perform abstinence through bone, manganese or coal. The source of this tradition is Syrian and is not authentic."
"150","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to perform ablution with rotten bone, manganese or coal. The narrator of this tradition, Ali bin Rabah, has not been proven to have heard it from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud."
"151","Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who was an Ansari, narrates this, he has stated this regarding the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade: ""One should perform istanja through bone, mange, or skin."" The authenticity of this tradition is not proven. The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman Majhool."
"152","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, \to cast iron or bone.\"" You have said this: \""These two things do not purify.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is \""Sahih\""."""""
"153","Abi ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the method of ablution, and he said: \Don't you find three stones? Two stones (to clean the sides of the exit) and one stone to (clean the exit).\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""""
"154","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once Saraqa bin Malik Mudalji passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the method of ablution. He should do istanja, which does not involve any Mangani, or do it through three pieces of wood or through three lumps of clay.”"
"155","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person needs to defecate, he should perform istanja through three sticks or three stones or three times by filling his fist with clay."" This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions and there are some differences in its traditions."
"156","Salama bin Wahram narrates: I heard Taaws narrate this: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “When a person starts defecating, he should respect the Qibla of Allah and not turn his back towards it, then purify himself with three stones or with three pieces of wood or with a handful of clay three times. Do it and then recite: All praise is due to Allah, the Exalted, Who has removed from me that which could have tormented me and left within me that which is beneficial to me.\""157"""""
"157","Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us: Harun ibn Ma‘ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Zam‘ah ibn Salih narrated to us from Salamah ibn Wahram and Ibn Tawus, from Tawus, from the Prophet (ﷺ) with this [hadith], mursal."
"158","The same tradition is narrated by Taos along with another chain of transmission."
"159","The same hadith is narrated by Taus along with another chain of transmission and it is narrated as his saying, he has not quoted this tradition as a \marfu'\"" hadith. A narrator named Ali narrates: I inquired from Sufyan: Has a narrator named Zamaa transmitted this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" hadith? So they answered: \""Yes!\"" Then I asked Salama about this"
"160","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""Maswak has ten virtues: it is a cause of God's pleasure, a cause of Satan's displeasure, a cause of happiness to the angels, a cause of health and beauty of the gums, removes tooth decay, sharpens vision, creates a fragrance in the mouth, reduces phlegm, brushing is a Sunnah and increases good deeds."" Shaykh Abul Hasan states: The narrator of this tradition, Maali bin Maimon, is weak and obsolete."
"161","Marwan Asfar narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, he made his camel sit facing the Qiblah and then sat down facing it and started to urinate. I said: \O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Is this not forbidden?\"" So he said: \""Yes! But it is forbidden to do this in the open air. When there is something obstructing you and the Qiblah"
"162","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, ""If we pour water on our private parts (during and after defecating), then we should turn our backs or face towards the Qibla."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: After that, I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one year before his appearance, and he was urinating facing the Qiblah. All the narrators of this hadeeth are trustworthy and a narrator named Ibn Shukar has narrated these words: ""Let us face the Qiblah or turn our backs."""
"163","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once it was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that some people do not like facing the Qibla while defecating and their backs, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to defecate in a place where the faeces were facing the Qibla. Imam Darqutni states: In the chain of transmission of this tradition, there is a narrator named Khalid bin Abu Salat between the narrator named Khalid and the narrator named Arak."
"164","Narrated Khalid: Those people were present with Umar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: ""Since I was young, I have never defecated facing the Qiblah."" Arak bin Malik was present with them. Arak said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated this: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know that some people disliked this, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this order about his toilet, so the toilet was turned towards the Qiblah. There is another tradition similar to this."
"165","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard about some people who disliked facing the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, so by the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) their places of defecation were turned towards the direction of the Qiblah. This tradition is more authentic. This tradition has also been narrated by some other narrators."
"166","Khalid bin Abu Salat narrates: I was sitting next to Umar bin Abdul Aziz during his caliphate, and Arak bin Malik was also sitting next to him. Umar ibn Abdul Aziz said: ""I have never turned my back towards the Qiblah while urinating or defecating for so long."" So Arak said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated this hadith to me. She says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the opinion of some people, the place of his stool was turned towards the Qiblah under the order of the Prophet (peace be upon him). The chain of transmission of this tradition is more reliable and it has the addition of a narrator named Khalid bin Abu Salat, and it is correct."
"167","Arak bin Malik narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, she says: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded: \Turn my toilet towards the Qiblah.\"" A narrator named Yahya bin Ishaq has narrated this: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought Tashrif and people were talking about the dislike of facing the Qiblah when urinating or defecating."""""
"168","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: On the order of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his toilet was turned towards the Qibla, when he found out that some people disliked it."
"169","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on some errand. Shaykh Abul Hasan (Imam Darqutni) says: The narrator named Isa bin Abu Isa Hanat is weak."
"170","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Do not face the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, and do not turn your back to it, but face the east or the west (according to Madinah Munawarah)."""
"171","Isa bin Abu 'Isa narrates: I said to Imam Sha'bi: I am very surprised at the saying of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) and the tradition narrated by Nafi' on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA). Imam Shaabi inquired: What have these two gentlemen stated? So I replied: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Do not turn your back or turn towards the Qiblah (at the time of need). While Nafi has quoted this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, he says: ""I saw the Holy Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him: He went to the bathroom to defecate, which was facing the Qiblah."" So Imam Sha'bi said this: ""As far as the saying of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) is concerned, it is about the desert, because there are some servants of Allah who pray in the desert, so you should not turn your back or turn towards them, but as far as the toilet built in houses is concerned, there is no prohibition to turn your back or face towards the Qibla."""
"172","Wasee bin Hibban narrates: I have heard Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrating this, he says: Once I climbed onto the roof of Sayyida Hafsa's (RA) house, at a time when I thought that no one would leave the house at that time. When I noticed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on two bricks facing towards the Holy House and performing his ablutions."
"173","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) brought a pot of water. This tradition has also been narrated along with other sources."
"174","Talha bin Nafi narrates: Sayyidna Abu Ayyub Ansari, Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari and Sayyidna Anas bin Malik Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them) have narrated this verse regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the verse is:) “In it are those who love it: they purify themselves well, and Allah loves those who purify themselves well.” is.” The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""O group of Ansar! Allah has highly praised you for attaining purity. What is your method of attaining purity?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution for prayer, we bathe in the state of Janabat."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Do you have any other method besides this?"" He said: ""No! But when one of us defecates, he likes it, he should defecate with water."" So the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""This will be the reason for it, you should adopt it."" The narrator of this tradition, Utbah bin Abu Hakim, is not authentic."
"175","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution with the water left by animals. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ibrahim bin Abi Hiyya, who is weak. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"176","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: It was asked: \O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution with the water left by the donkeys?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Perform ablution (also) with water from the hooves of animals.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Ibn Abi Habiba"
"177","This tradition is narrated from Dawud bin Husain along with another chain of transmission."
"178","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The price of a dog is impure and he himself is even more impure than that.\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"179","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the houses of some Ansaris, the houses that were before their houses (he did not visit them there), so these people were surprised by this, they said: \O Messenger of Allah! You have visited the house of so-and-so and did not visit our house?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The reason for this is: There is a dog in your house.\"" He said: \""There is a cat in their house.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The cat is among the beasts.\"" Narrator Isa bin Musayb is unique in narrating this tradition and these hadiths are reliable in narrating."""""
"180","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""A cat is a beast."" In one tradition, the word ""alhar"" is used for cat."
"181","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish, that person should wash it seven times."" This tradition is ""correct""."
"182","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish, he should empty the dish and wash the dish seven times."" The authenticity of this tradition is authentic and authentic, and all its narrators are authentic."
"183","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, this hadith was narrated about a dog: When a dog puts its mouth into a vessel, he says: ""The contents of it should be washed away, and the vessel should be washed seven times."" This hadith is correct and ""suspended""."
"184","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, the way to purify it is to wash it seven times, the first of which is to be cleaned with mud."""
"185","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The method of purifying a person's vessel, when a dog has put its mouth in it, is this: He should wash it seven times and clean it with mud the first time."" Imam Uza'i attended the service of Ibn Sirin when he was ill. Imam Uza'i has not heard hadiths from Ibn Sirin."
"186","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The way to purify a vessel, when a dog has put its mouth in it, is this: This vessel should be washed seven times, the first of which should be cleaned with mud. If a cat has put its mouth in it, it should be washed once or twice."" This doubt belongs to the narrator named Qara, and this tradition is authentic."
"187","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, wash it seven times and clean it with mud the seventh time."""
"188","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"189","The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains the words: \The first time to be cleansed with mud.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"190","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, wash it seven times and the first time through mud."" This hadith is ""correct""."
"191","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What is the benefit of this to the people?\"" Then the Prophet (PBUH) allowed dogs to be kept to protect the hunting dogs and goats. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"192","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish, that person should wash it seven times and one of them should clean it with sand."" The narrator of this tradition is the son of Jarudzid and is ""abandoned""."
"193","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about dogs: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, a man should wash it three times (perhaps these words are:) five times or perhaps (these words are:) seven times."""
"194","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: ""That person should wash it three times (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words:) wash it five times or wash it seven times."" The narrator named Abdul Wahab is unique in quoting this tradition from a narrator named Ismail and this narrator is a ""Mutaruk Hadith"". Other narrators have narrated this tradition with reference to a narrator named Ismail and it has these words: ""Wash it seven times."" And this tradition is correct."
"195","This same tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission, in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \You should wash it seven times.\"" This tradition is more authentic."""""
"196","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, you should pour out the water in it and then wash it three times."" This tradition is ""suspended"" and no one has narrated it in this way (as a ""suspended"" tradition) except for a narrator named Abdul Malik."
"197","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: ""If a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, a man should drain the water in it and wash the vessel three times."""
"198","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes a cat would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would hold out a vessel to it and it would drink water from it, and then he would perform ablution with the water from the cat's paws. A narrator named Abu Bakr narrates: The narrator of this tradition is Yaqub, this is Qazi Abu Yusuf, and the narrator named Abd Rabbah is Abdullah bin Saeed Maqbri, who is weak."
"199","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu has this saying about the cat's dung: \This water should be drained away and this vessel should be washed once (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) twice.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""""
"200","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates this about Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, he said: ""When a cat puts its mouth in a vessel, you should drain the water in it and wash it once."""
"201","Muhammad bin Sireen narrates the saying of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu: He said this about cats: ""If it puts its mouth into a vessel, Sayyidna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Wash it once and drain the water in it."""
"202","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said this about a cat: ""When it puts its mouth in a vessel, a man should wash it seven times."" The narrator of this hadith is not Laith bin Abu Salim Hafiz and this hadith is ""suspended"", and is not authentically transmitted by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira RA, it is more likely that it is Ata's own saying."
"203","Hasan bin Ali narrates: I heard Ata narrate this: He said this about cats: ""When it puts its mouth in a vessel, a man should wash it seven times."""
"204","Saeed bin Musayb says: \A man should wash it twice (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) three times.\"""""""
"205","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, the way to purify it is this: it should be washed seven times, and the first time it should be cleaned with mud, and the command about the cat is this, it should be washed once or twice."" This doubt belongs to the narrator named Qara. Narrator Abu Bakr has narrated this: Narrator Abu Asim narrated this hadith as a “marfu’ hadith, while other narrators narrated the command about the dog as a “marfu’ hadith and the command to muzzle the cat as a “mawafuk” hadith."
"206","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says this about a cat: ""When it puts its mouth in a vessel, you wash it once (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these words are:) wash it twice."" This hadith is likewise narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah as a ""suspended"" hadith."
"207","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""The vessel will be washed when a cat puts it in its mouth, just as it is washed when a dog puts it in its mouth."" This hadith is ""suspended"" and is not authentically proven from Sayyidina Abu Huraira. Anxiety is found in some traditions of the narrator named Yahya bin Ayyub."
"208","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a cat puts its mouth in it, the vessel will be washed in the same way as it is washed when a dog's mouth is put in it."" Shaykh (Imam Darqutni) says: This hadith is not authentic as ""marfu'"" and it is more authentic as the saying of Sayyidina Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu, and there is also disagreement about this."
"209","This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another chain of transmission."""""
"210","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \The vessel in which the cat puts its mouth should be washed seven times.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"" and not authentically transmitted."""""
"211","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"212","The sons of Taos narrate this about their father: He used to wash the pot seven times, even after a cat's mouth, like a dog's mouth. Ibn Jaraj narrates: I asked Ata: What is the ruling of the cat? So he said: \It is like a dog.\"" Or perhaps he said: \""It's worse than that.\"""""""
"213","Mujahid says about putting a cat's mouth in a vessel: \Wash this vessel seven times.\"""""""
"214","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to perform ablution from the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water. This tradition is \correct\""."""""
"215","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution using the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water."
"216","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This (cat) is not impure, but it is like the (animals) living in the house."" This saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is about the cat."
"217","It was narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA): Once a cat ate some of Harisa, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) later ate some of it and said: ""I saw the Prophet (PBUH), he used to perform ablution with cat's dung (water)."" The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it is ""suspended"" until Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"218","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour the pot towards the cat and the cat would drink from it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution through the cat's hooves."
"219","Narrated Sayyidah Kabsha bint Ka'b, who was the wife of one of the sons of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah: Once Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah entered the house of Ansari, and this woman kept ablution water for him. Meanwhile, a cat came to him to drink water from it, so Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) poured the pot towards him, and the cat drank the water. That woman narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Qutada (RA) saw me looking at him with great attention, he inquired: \O my niece! Are you surprised at this?\"" The woman narrates: I answered: \""Yes!\"" So Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) said: \""The Prophet (PBUH) said this: This (cat) is not impure"
"220","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him): Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) (or perhaps Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him) was asked about the cat's hoof, and he said: \It is among the beasts"
"221","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) searched for water for ablution, but they did not find it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: ""Is there even a little water anywhere?"" (He was present), he was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet. The narrator narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his blessed hand on the vessel in which there was water, then he said: ""Invoke the name of Allah and start ablution."" Narrator narrates: I saw springs of water coming out from between your fingers and people started performing ablution, until all the people performed ablution. A narrator named Thabit narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Anas: ""How many were you at that time?"" Sayyiduna Anas (RA) replied: ""(We) were about seventy people."""
"222","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""He who does not mention the name of Allah in the beginning, it is as if he did not perform ablution, and he who does not perform ablution, it is as if he did not pray, and he who does not love me, it is as if he did not believe in me, and he who does not love the Ansar, it is as if he does not love me."""
"223","Rabi' bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \There is no ablution for a person who does not recite the name of Allah at the beginning of it (i.e. does not recite Bismillah).\"""""""
"224","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch (the bowl of ablution) he used to recite Bismillah first. A narrator named Abu Badr has described this (that is, these words are in the hadith): \When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up for ablution"
"225","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates his father's statement regarding his grandmother: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution, and no ablution for a person who does not begin with the name of Allah (i.e. does not recite Bismillah), and a person does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and a person does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar."""
"226","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"227","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""There is no prayer without ablution, and whoever does not recite the name of Allah at the beginning, he does not have ablution, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and whoever does not love the Ansar, in fact, does not believe in me."""
"228","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I heard the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam saying: ""The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer, and the person who does not recite Bismillah at the beginning, that person does not have his ablution."""
"229","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, narrate this, he says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: ""The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer, and the person who does not say ""Bismillah"" at the beginning, does not have his ablution."""
"230","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"231","Sayyiduna Abdullah (Bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: ""When a person starts performing ablution, he should recite Bismillah first, because this will purify his whole body. If he does not recite Bismillah before performing ablution, then only that part of him that has water will be purified. There is no god but Allah, and Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the special servant and messenger of Allah, when he recites this, the gates of heaven will be opened for him.” The narrator of this tradition, Yahya bin Hashim, is weak."
"232","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah (i.e. Bismillah), his whole body is purified, and whoever performs ablution and does not recite the name of Allah (i.e. does not recite Bismillah), then only that part of him on which he performed ablution becomes pure."""
"233","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah at the beginning of ablution, his whole body becomes pure."" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: ""Whoever performs ablution and does not mention the name of Allah at the beginning, only his specific parts are purified."""
"234","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""For one who cannot find water, the Prophet is a means of ablution."" Imam Abu Muhammad narrates: This means the Prophet who is not intoxicating. The Imam has also stated this: In this tradition, the narrator named Musayb has had an illusion and this illusion is in two places, one is that he has mentioned Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and the other is that he has mentioned the Prophet (PBUH). In this tradition, there is a difference in some words regarding the disaster."
"235","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Musaib as a ""suspended"" hadith, not as a ""marfu'"" hadith. More authentically, this is proven: This is the saying of Ikrima, it is not a hadith ""reported"" to the Holy Prophet, nor is it authentic to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas. The narrator named Masib is weak."
"236","Narrated Ikramah: \Nabeez is a means of ablution for a person who does not have anything to perform ablution other than Nabeez (i.e. he does not have water).\"""""""
"237","Ikramah states: ""Whoever finds nothing else besides Nabeez, he can perform ablution through Nabeez."" Imam Uza'i states: ""If that Prophet is intoxicating, then a person will not perform ablution through it."" A narrator named Abdullah narrates: My father narrated: ""Whatever cannot be called water, my favorite opinion is this: A man should not perform ablution through it, and I like it more: A man should perform tayammum instead of performing ablution through the Prophet."""
"238","Narrated Ikramah: ""Through water, one can perform ablution, who does not have access to water."""
"239","Ikramah states: \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""""
"240","Isa bin Ubaid narrates: I heard Ikrima, he was asked about a person: Who does not get water. Ikramah said: \That person should perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""""
"241","Ikrimah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through water.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Ibn Muharr"
"242","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person does not get water, and if he finds Nabid, he should perform ablution through Nabid."" The narrator of this hadeeth is Aban, son of Abu Ayyash and it is a ""Mutaruk Hadith"" while the narrator Muja'ah is ""weak"". More authentically this is proven: this is Ikrima's opinion and not a ""marfu'"" hadith."
"243","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates this statement from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him): On the night of the meeting with the Jinn, he performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a nabid, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with it. A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is not considered authentic. There is also a saying: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) was not present with the Prophet (PBUH) on the night of the meeting with the jinn. Alqamah bin Qais has narrated it in the same way. Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah and other narrators have narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu, he says: \I was not present on the night of the meeting with the jinn.\"""""""
"244","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Mas’ud (RA): Once he went out with the Prophet (PBUH), it was the night when he met the jinn, and the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: “O Ibn Mas’ud! Do you have water?” Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \I have Nabeez in a vessel.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Pour it over me.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it and said: \""It is also something to drink and purification can also be achieved from it.\"" A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is unique in narrating this tradition and it is a weak narrator."""""
"245","Alqamah bin Qays narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him: ""When the representatives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet, was any of you present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that night?"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu replied: ""No!"" This hadith is authentic regarding its transmission from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud."
"246","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz narrated from us, he said: Ali bin Al-Jaad narrated from us, he was informed by Shu’ba, he from Amr bin Murrah, he said: I said to Abu Ubaidah, may God be pleased with him: “Did Abdullah bin Mas’ud participate in the night of the jinn?” He said: \No.\"""""""
"247","Narrated Amr bin Murrah: I asked Abu Ubaidah: ""Was Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud RA the night he met the jinn?"" So they answered: ""No!"" It is narrated in another hadith: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: On the night of the meeting with the jinn, the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him: ""Do you have water?"" So they said: ""No!"" You then inquired: ""Do you have a Prophet?"" The narrator says: I think, the hadith has these words: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu replied: ""Yes!"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through this prophet. Imam Darqutni states: This hadith is not proven in two contexts, which I have already mentioned."
"248","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but its narrators have been cross-examined."
"249","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired on the night of his meeting with the jinn: \Do you have any water?\"" So they said: \""No!\"" I have a prophet. The narrator narrates: Then this prophet was brought and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through him."""""
"250","Abu Wail narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of his meeting with the jinn. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) asked me at some part of the night: \O Ibn Mas'ud! Do you have water?\"" I said: \""No! By Allah! O Messenger of Allah! I have only Nabeez in the vessel.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The date palm is pure and its water is purifying.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it. A narrator named Hussain bin Ubaidullah used to invent and narrate traditions on the authority of Taqqa narrators."""""
"251","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me. He said: ""Take a vessel of water with you."" Then you continued walking, I also stayed with you, then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu mentioned the incident of the meeting with the jinn. Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When I poured water on you from this vessel, it was Nabeez. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have made a mistake, I have brought Nabeez."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The date palm is sweet and its water is sweet."" A narrator named Hasan bin Qutiba is unique in narrating this tradition, and both Hasan bin Tasheba and a narrator named Muhammad bin Isa are weak."
"252","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the night of my meeting with the jinn, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to bring water for ablution. This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Thaqafi on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu: It is unknown. According to one view his name is Amr and according to another view his name is Abdullah bin Amr."
"253","Abu Khaldah narrates: I asked Abul Aaliyah: A person who does not have water with him, but he has Nabeez, can he perform Ghusl Janabat through this Nabeez? So Abul Alia replied: ""No!"" So I mentioned to him the hadith about the meeting with the jinn, and he said: ""The Nabeez that is made with you is evil. What it was was raisins and water."""
"254","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He did not think there was anything wrong with performing ablution through the Prophet."
"255","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He said: \There is no harm in performing ablution through water.\"""""""
"256","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution, and there is no ablution for a person who does not recite Bismillah at the beginning."""
"257","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"258","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water for ablution, he performed ablution with it once, and then he said: ""This is the method of ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer."" Then he called for water and performed ablution twice with it, then said: ""This is the method of ablution for a person who will get a double reward for performing ablution."" Then he stayed for a while, then he asked for water, then he performed ablution three times. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""This is my way of ablution and that of the Prophets before me."""
"259","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"260","The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA), but some of its narrators have been declared weak."
"261","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution once and said: ""This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer."" Then he performed ablution twice, twice, and said: ""This is the way of performing ablution for a person to whom Allah will reward him twice."" Then he performed ablution three times and said: ""This is my method of ablution and that of the Messengers before me."" Narrator named Musayb bin Al-Khalya is unique in narrating this tradition from Hafs bin Maysara and this narrator named Musayb is weak."
"262","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): “Whoever performs ablution once, this is the method of ablution that is necessary, and whoever performs ablution twice, he will receive double the reward, and whoever performs ablution three times, then this is my method and that of the prophets who came before me.”"
"263","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water and performed ablution with it once, and then said: ""This is the method of ablution. Whoever does not perform ablution in this way, his prayer will not be accepted."" Then he performed ablution twice, then he said: ""This is the method of ablution for a person who performs ablution in this way, Allah will give him a double reward."" Then he performed ablution three times, and then he said: ""This is my way and that of the prophets who came before me."""
"264","Ubaidullah bin Abu Rafi' narrated this statement of his father: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution three times, and I saw him perform ablution once."
"265","Thabit Samali narrates: I asked Imam Abu Ja'far (Imam Muhammad Baqir) this: Has Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated this hadith to you? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once, once and twice, twice and three times, then Imam Abu Ja'far (i.e. Imam Baqir) replied: \Yes!\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"266","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, who was shown the way to call the call to prayer in a dream, narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and washed both feet twice. Ibn Ayaina narrated it in the same way, by the way, its narrator is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd al-Mazni, may God be pleased with him, and these are not the Companions who were taught how to give the call to prayer in a dream."
"267","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, may God be pleased with him, who was shown the way to call the Adhan in a dream, narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and both feet twice, and wiped his head twice."
"268","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head and washed both his feet twice.\"""""""
"269","The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his face three times and washed both his arms twice.\"""""""
"270","Amr bin Yahya narrates the statement of his father: Amr bin Abu Hasan Mazni came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu. Amr ibn Abu Hasan requested: ""Can you show us this? How did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution?"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu replied: ""Yes!"" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah called for a vessel of water, he poured water from this vessel on his right hand and washed his right hand three times, then he poured water from the vessel on both his hands and washed both hands three times, then he put both his hands in the vessel and took a chawl of water and rinsed through it and poured water into his nose, then he cleaned his nose with water in a chawl three times, then he washed his face three times, each arm up to the elbows. Washed, then took some water and anointed the head with it, they moved their hands from front to back, then from back to front, then they washed both feet up to the ankles."
"271","Hamran narrates: One day Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani asked for water for ablution, then he performed ablution, washed both hands three times, then rinsed, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his right arm up to the elbow three times and then washed his left arm in the same way, then he wiped his head, then he washed his right foot up to the ankle three times and then his left foot in the same way. Washed, and narrated this: ""I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he performed ablution in the same way as I have performed ablution, then the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: 'Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine and then gets up and performs two nafls, in which he is not lost in his thoughts, Allah Almighty will forgive his past sins.'"" Ibn Shahab Zahri narrates: Our scholars have stated: ""This is the way to perform ablution properly for prayer."""
"272","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he used to pour water up to his elbows. The narrator of this tradition, Ibn Aqeel, is not authentic."
"273","A narrator named Ubaidullah has narrated this on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Rafi': When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would move his ring (while washing his hands). Both the narrator of this tradition, Muammar and his father, are weak and this tradition is not authentic."
"274","Hamran narrates: He heard Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu, Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu said: ""You people come forward, I will perform ablution according to the way of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and show you people."" Then Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) washed his face, washed his arms up to the elbows, until they touched the edges of his shoulders, then he wiped his head, and passed his hands over his ears and beard, and then washed both his feet."
"275","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Grinding and pouring water into the nose is an obligatory part of ablution.\"""""""
"276","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: ""This is a part of ablution, without which ablution is not complete."" Narrator Issam is unique in narrating this tradition and he is delusional about it. The correct tradition is that narrated by a narrator named Ibn Jarij as a ""Mursal"" Hadith on the authority of Salman bin Musa, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose."" Imam Darqutni states: I think that the narrator named Essam narrated this hadith with reference to his memory and it got mixed up on him, and he became suspicious of the authenticity of this hadith which was narrated as the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding Sayyida Aisha, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"277","As for the hadeeth narrated by Ibn Jarij on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, which is about ablution and putting water in the nose, then it is: Ibn Jarij narrates: Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever performs ablution"
"278","Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose."""
"279","Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose."""
"280","Sulaiman ibn Musa al-Shami narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this, followed by the previous hadith."
"281","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose."" The narrator of this tradition is Muhammad bin Azhar Zaeef and this tradition is incorrect, the ""Mursal"" tradition that was narrated before it is more authentic. The rest Allah knows best."
"282","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It is Sunnah to rinse (during ablution) and pour water into the nose. The narrator of this tradition is Ismail bin Muslim \weak\""."""""
"283","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA): One day he called for water for ablution and then called some of the companions of the Prophet (RA), then he poured water on his left hand through his right hand and washed it three times. He rinsed three times, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, three times, then he wiped his head, then he washed both his feet and cleaned them well, then he narrated: ""I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution in the same way as you have just seen me perform ablution, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution and performs ablution well, then performs two rak'ahs of prayer, then his sins are as if they were on the day when his mother gave birth to him."""
"284","Basar bin Saeed narrates: Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, came to the ""Maqeed"", he asked for water for ablution, rinsed, then poured water into his nose and then washed his face three times, then washed both arms three times, then washed his feet three times, then wiped his head and said: ""I remember this about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he performed ablution in the same way."" Then Syedna Uthman Ghani (RA) addressed the audience and said: ""O Gentlemen! Is it like this?"" So these gentlemen answered: ""Yes!"" This was said by some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who were present there at that time. This hadith is authentic, but it is not safe to delay wiping the head. One narrator is unique in narrating it while other narrators have narrated it along with their authority. All the narrators have narrated the same thing: Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may God be pleased with him) washed all the limbs three times, then said: ""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution in this way."" These narrators did not narrate anything other than this. On the contrary, a narrator named Waqi' has narrated this with reference to Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) washed each organ three times in ablution. Some other narrators have also narrated it in the same context."
"285","Abu Anas narrates: Once Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) performed ablution in the sitting room, while some companions (RA) were present with him. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) washed each organ three times and then inquired: \Didn't you see the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution in the same way?\"" So these gentlemen answered: \""Yes!\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""""
"286","Abu Wail narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, he performed ablution and washed both hands three times, then washed his face three times, then rinsed his nose three times, poured water into his nose three times, then washed both arms three times, then wiped his head and the outside and inside of both ears, and then washed both feet three times, then he crossed his fingers, and when he had washed his face, he then washed his face three times. He had also shaved his beard, then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrated this: ""I saw the Prophet (PBUH), he performed (ablution) in the same way as you have seen me perform (ablution)."" This hadith is narrated with the same words, but at one point in this hadith, the narrator is delusional, because it mentions the beginning of ablution by washing the face and this is before washing the face, rinsing and putting water in the nose, while the narrator named Abdul Rahman has narrated this tradition along with the same chain of transmission and it mentions the beginning of ablution by washing the face and putting water in the nose and this process is before washing the face."
"287","Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, first he washed both hands three times, then he rinsed, he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head and then he wiped the inside and outside of both ears, he shaved his beard three times and then he washed both feet, he also washed his toes three times. and said: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform (ablution) in the same way as I have performed this (ablution).\"" The words of these two traditions are very close."""""
"288","Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and after washing his arms, he wiped his head with a cotton swab."
"289","Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to visit us, and when he performed ablution, he would wipe his head with the remaining water after washing both arms and wipe in this way. After that, a narrator named Abdullah bin Dawud showed him by wiping and bringing his two hands from the back of the head to the front and then moving both hands from the front to the back of the head."
"290","A narrator named Ziyad narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) and asked him about performing ablution and said: \Should I start with the right hand or should I start with the left hand?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali reprimanded him and then he called for water and (doing ablution) washed his left hand before his right hand."""""
"291","Narrated Ziyad: A man asked Sayyiduna Ali: ""Can I wash my left hand before my right hand during ablution?"" So Sayyiduna Ali rebuked him, then he called for water and washed his left hand before his right hand."
"292","A narrator named Ziyad narrates: Sayyiduna Ali was asked: \Sayyidna Abu Huraira always washes the right organ first in ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali called for water and started from the left side while doing ablution."""""
"293","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""When I perform ablution, I do not care with which organ (right or left) I have started?"""
"294","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"295","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""I do not care about this, when I start ablution, I start with my left hand before my right hand."""
"296","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Abbas may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: \There is nothing wrong with that. You wash (in ablution) both your feet before your arms.\"" This tradition is \""transmitted\"" and it is not proven."""""
"297","It was narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA): He was asked about a person who washes his left side first while performing ablution, then Sayyidna Abdullah (RA) said: \There is nothing wrong with that.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"298","A narrator named Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: “He first washed his two hands while doing ablution, then rinsed them three times and poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times and then washed both feet three times, and then said: ‘Whoever likes to see the way of ablution of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, let him. Look at this way.'"" Shuaib, the narrator, has narrated these words: (Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him) said: A narrator named Abu Hanifa has narrated this hadith with reference to a narrator named Khalid, in it he has quoted these words: Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, wiped his head three times, while a group of Muhadditheen have also narrated this tradition in other contexts, and it mentions wiping his head once. Among these other muhaddiths, only the narrator named Hajjaj has been delusional at one point, he has mentioned the narrator named Amr Dhamar instead of the narrator named Abd Khair. According to our knowledge, no narrator except Imam Abu Hanifa has mentioned wiping the head three times. Imam Abu Hanifa has narrated something different from other narrators in his tradition, while on the other hand, his own opinion about the order of wiping is also different from this tradition, which he has narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, with reference to Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, because Imam Abu Hanifa also states this: ""It is Sunnah to wipe the head once in ablution."" This has been narrated by Ibrahim bin Abu Yahya and Qazi Abu Yusuf along with their chain of transmission from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"299","Abd Khair narrates: One day Sayyiduna Ali (RA) sat outside in the field after performing the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: ""Bring water for ablution!"" The servant brought water in a pot and brought a saucer with him. We were looking at Sayyiduna Ali, he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both his hands, and then he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand and washed his hands, he did this three times. A narrator named Abd Khair narrates: In each of these times, he did not put his hand inside the vessel, but poured water from the vessel and washed both hands three times. Then he put his right hand into the pot and (taking water) rinsed through it and poured water into his nose. He wiped his nose from inside with his left hand, he did this three times, then he put his right hand into the pot and washed his face three times, then he washed his right arm up to the elbow three times and his left arm up to the elbow three times, then he put his right hand into the pot until his hand was filled with water, then he raised it with the water and then turned his left hand over it and both hands He wiped his head once, then he poured water on his right foot three times with his right hand and washed that foot three times with his left hand. He poured water on his left foot three times with his right hand and washed it with his left hand. If he sees the way of ablution of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then this is the way of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some narrators have copied some of the words of this tradition more or less, but the meaning of all of them is close to each other and is authentically proven."
"300","Abd Khair narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed all his limbs three times while performing ablution and took fresh water for his head.\"""""""
"301","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him: When he performed ablution, he washed his hands three times, poured water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth three times, then washed his face three times, washed each of his two arms three times, wiped his head three times, then washed his feet three times, then said: ""I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution in this way."" The narrator of this tradition, Ishaq Yahya, is weak."
"302","Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, then he rinsed first, then he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, then he trimmed his beard three times, then he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head three times, he washed both feet three times, and then he narrated this matter to the Prophet, peace be upon him. I have seen him doing (ablution) like that.”"
"303","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He called for water for ablution, then washed both his hands three times, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times and said: ""I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution in the same way. He also said: 'Whoever performs ablution less than that It would also be permissible to do so."
"304","Narrated by Ibn Daraa: I entered the house of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and he heard my voice saying that I was performing ablution, so he called out: ""O Muhammad!"" I said: ""I am here!"" He said: ""Shall I not tell you the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet?"" I replied: ""Yes!"" So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: ""I remember well about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, water was brought for him, he was sitting in the courtyard at that time, he rinsed three times, poured water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times, and (then Sayyidna Uthman, may God be pleased with him) said this. Ki: ""This is how the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. I wanted to show you this."""
"305","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He performed ablution in a maqa'id (open space), in Madinah the maqa'id (open space) is where the funeral prayer is performed near the mosque. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani first washed his hands three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then rinsed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times. A person greeted him, he was still performing ablution, Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani did not respond to the greeting until he finished performing ablution, when he finished, he presented an excuse to him while talking to him and said: \I did not respond to the greeting because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever performs ablution in this way and does not utter a word during ablution and this (After ablution) read: \""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"
"306","Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: ""While performing ablution, he washed each organ three times and wiped his head and both ears three times and said: 'This is the way of ablution of the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, I like to show you this.'"""
"307","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever performs ablution and washes his hands three times, pours water into his nose three times, rinses his mouth three times, washes his face and both arms three times, wipes his head three times, washes his feet three times, then recites: ‘I testify that there is no god but Allah, and Sayyidna Muhammad. (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) is His special servant and messenger.''"
"308","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him): Once he came with some of his companions and sat in a muqa'id (open space), he asked for water for ablution, then he washed both his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, poured water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, wiped his head once, then washed his two feet three times, and then said this Ki: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution in the same way. I was already in a state of ablution"
"309","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to wash each organ twice while performing ablution."
"310","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) used to perform ablution twice."
"311","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution for prayer, he would move the ring on his finger."
"312","Ghulam Safina, the slave of Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with one \Mud\"" of water and performed Ghusl with one \""Sa'\"" of water."""""
"313","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with about one mudd of water and performed ghusl with about one saa of water."
"314","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with two \liters\"" of water and one \""Sa'\"" with eight liters of water. A narrator named Musa bin Nasr is unique in narrating this tradition and this Sahib is weak."""""
"315","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Ten things are part of nature: trimming the moustache, growing the beard, brushing the nose, cleaning the nose with water, clipping the nails, cleaning the armpit hair, cleaning the pubic hair, and defecating with water."" A narrator named Zakariya has narrated this: A narrator named Musab has narrated this: ""I have forgotten the tenth thing, but it must be washed."" The narrator named Al-Khajri has quoted this with reference to the narrator named Zakariya and stated: The word ""Intaqas al-Ma'a"" used in the hadith means to withdraw through water. A narrator named Musab bin Shaba is unique in narrating this. Narrators Abu Bashar and Sulaiman have narrated this differently, they have narrated this hadith on the authority of Talaq bin Habib, as their own words, and have not narrated this hadith as a ""marfu'"" hadith."
"316","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Harith bin Jaz Zubaydi (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \For (some) heels and soles are the destruction of Hell.\"""""""
"317","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he used to rub his toes (toes) and touch his heels, and he used to say: ""What do you rub between your toes, Allah will not enter the fire between them, and some heels are doomed to hell."""
"318","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Make a cross between your fingers, Allah will not cross between them on the Day of Resurrection with fire.”"
"319","This is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Rifa'a bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyidna Rifa'a (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Malik bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) are brothers and participated in the Battle of Badr. Sayyidna Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were sitting with the Holy Prophet (may Allah's prayers and peace be upon him). He prayed facing the Qiblah, when he finished the prayer, he came and greeted the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and also greeted the people present. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""You must go back and pray, because you did not actually pray."" This person started to pray again, we kept examining his prayer carefully, we didn't understand what he did wrong? When he finished the prayer, he came and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those present. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""It is obligatory upon you, you go and pray again. You have not actually prayed."" A narrator named Hammam narrates: I do not know what is mentioned in the hadith, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him twice or instructed him three times, then the person said: ""What have I missed? I do not know which part of my prayer you are invalidating?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one's prayer is complete until he performs ablution well as Allah Almighty has commanded him. He should first wash his face, then wash both arms up to the elbows, then wipe his head, wash both feet up to the ankles, mention the greatness of Allah, praise Him, then recite Surah Al-Fatihah, then recite what is his destiny."" I said, let him recite (parts of the Qur'an) that he finds easy, then say the Takbeer and go into Ruku, and place both his hands on his knees until his joints are satisfied and wide, then he should recite 'Sami'Allah Liman Hamda' and stand up straight, until his back is straight, and every bone is in its place, then he should say the Takbeer and go into Sajdah, and keep his forehead fixed. A narrator named Hammam has sometimes quoted these words here: ""He should place his forehead on the ground, until his joints are relaxed and wide, then he should sit on his back saying the Takbeer, and keep his back straight."" After that, he explained the way of praying in the four rak'ahs in the same way, until he explained it completely and (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one's prayer is complete until he does this."""
"320","Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated this on the authority of Sayyida Rabi bint Mu’awz: He asked Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) about the manner of ablution of the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him), and Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) replied: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit her, she used to keep ablution water for the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him). Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Once I came to this woman, and she took out a vessel in front of me and told me: “In this vessel, I used to draw water for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to perform ablution. He washed both arms, then wiped his head from front to back and from back to front, then he washed both feet, then this woman said: ""Your cousin also came to me, this woman meant Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, so I told him about this, so he said: ""I find two things in the book of God and two things to be wiped."" Let's do: I inquired of this lady: ""How much water was in that pot?"" So they replied: ""As much as a 'Hashmi Madd' is, as much as a common Madd and a quarter Madd."" A narrator named Abbas bin Yazid narrated this: This woman narrated the following on the authority of the Holy Prophet: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, washed his face before ablution and pouring water into his nose, while the people of Badr narrated this, including Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani and Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. They used to do it before washing and this is also the common practice of people."
"321","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" The narrator narrated it as follows: However, this is an illusion on the part of the narrator, because the correct thing is: It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a “suspended” tradition."
"322","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" The narrator has quoted this tradition as ""Marfu'"" tradition and it is his illusion. This is the correct thing, it is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as his own saying. The narrator of this tradition, Qasim bin Yahya, is weak."
"323","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" The narrator has quoted this tradition as a ""marfu' hadith in the same way, but this is his illusion, while other narrators have also quoted it as a ""marfu' tradition with reference to Ubayd Allah, but this is also their illusion. In addition, the narrator has also been delusional in mentioning a narrator named Thauri, however, along with another chain of transmission, this tradition is from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a ""moquf"" tradition. It is portable."
"324","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""""
"325","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Wasti narrated that Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to him, he said that Abu Bakr told him that Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated from Ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to wipe both ears and say, \These are the two parts of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a \""suspended\"" hadith."""""
"326","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to wipe both ears and say: \These two are part of the head.\"""""""
"327","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"328","Hilal bin Usamah narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) say: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"330","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Muhammad bin Fazl Muhammad bin Fazl bin Atiya"
"331","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"332","The same tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions, in which the narrator is delusional at some point. The subject of this tradition also exists, but the narrator narrating it is obsolete. However, more accurately, this tradition is transmitted as a \messenger\"" tradition from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to a narrator named Sulaiman bin Musa."""""
"333","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"334","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \(When performing ablution) rinse and pour water into the nose and the two ears are part of the head (ie the ears will be wiped like the head).\"" The narrator of this hadith is Rabi bin Badr."""""
"335","Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"336","Sulaiman bin Musa quoted the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"337","The same tradition is also narrated with reference to Sulaiman bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"338","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Solomon bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"339","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Both ears are part of the head."" Narrator named Ali bin Asim has been deceived in quoting this tradition, he has narrated it from the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the tradition that has been narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurij before him is more authentic."
"340","Sayyida Aisha Sadiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose, and both ears are part of the head, (meaning they will also be anointed)."" It is quoted as such by the narrator, but it is more authentic to be the ""Messenger""."
"341","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person performs ablution, he should rinse and put water in his nose and both ears are part of the head."""
"342","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated the same thing with reference to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but in it there are these words:"
"343","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Grinding and putting water in the nose is a part of ablution without which ablution is not complete, and the two ears are part of the head (i.e. they will be wiped over both of them)."" The narrator of this hadith is Jabir Zaeef, and there is a difference of opinion in this hadith regarding quoting from him. A narrator named Huqam bin Abdullah has narrated it as a Mursal tradition and this seems to be more accurate."
"344","A narrator named Ata has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Grinding and pouring water into the nose is one of the acts of ablution, without which ablution is not complete, and the two ears are part of the head."" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Umar bin Qays along with his chain of command as a ""suspended"" hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."
"345","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: ""In ablution, the two ears are part of the head (i.e. both ears will also be wiped) and in Ihram they are part of the face (i.e. they will not be covered)."" The narrator of this tradition, Umar bin Qais, is weak. This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (Radi Allahu Anhu) along with another chain of transmission, but there is some disagreement in it."
"346","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""It is Sunnah to rinse and pour water into the nose, and the two ears are part of the head."" The narrator of this hadith is Ismail bin Muslim weak and Qasim bin Ghassan is also weak like him. Ali bin Hashim has some differences in quoting this hadith, he narrated it along with his chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA), but this is also not authentic."
"347","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person performs ablution, he should rinse and put water in his nose and both ears are part of the head."" This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
"348","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"349","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"350","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and one of its narrators is Muhammad bin Ziyad Matrook Hadith. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated as a \suspended\"" hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."""""
"351","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The same tradition has also been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."""""
"352","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rinse (while performing ablution) and pour water into the nose, both ears are part of the head. One of the narrators of this hadith, Amr Ibn Husayn, and the other narrator, Ibn Alashah, are weak."
"353","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition"
"354","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Bakhtari bin Ubayd Zaeef and his father is unknown."""""
"355","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): ""Both ears are part of the head."" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Ali Ibn Jafar as a ""marfu'"" hadith, but it is more correct, this hadith is ""suspended"", the narrator of this hadith, Hasan, has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"356","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"". Some other narrators have followed suit. The same hadith is also narrated from Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (may Allah be pleased with him)."""""
"357","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Both ears are part of the head."" (He has also stated this:) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the corners of both eyes and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe his blessed head once. The narrator of this tradition, Shahr bin Haushab, is not authentic. A narrator named Sulaiman bin Harb has narrated this tradition as a ""suspended"" tradition and this narrator is trustworthy and authentic."
"358","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu has quoted the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"359","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) has quoted this saying of the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words: Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" That is"
"360","It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" The narrators have narrated it in the same way with reference to the narrator named Hamad, however, the narrator named Sulaiman bin Harb has narrated something differently. These Sahibs are trustworthy and Hafiz."
"361","A narrator named Shahr bin Hushab has narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA): Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) narrated the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: When the Prophet (SAW) used to perform ablution, he used to wipe the corners of his eyes with water. Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu also stated: ""Both ears are part of the head."" Sulaiman bin Harb has stated: ""Both ears are part of the head."" This is the saying of Sayyidina Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu, who says something other than this (i.e. declares it as Hadith) then he has changed. Here the narrator Solomon said something else, which meant: He has made a mistake. Some other narrators have narrated something different from this, they have narrated this on the authority of Anas (RA): When the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution, he used to wash the corners of both eyes with his fingers. However, he did not mention the two ears in this tradition."
"362","Daalaj ibn Ahmad narrates: I asked Musa ibn Haroon about this hadith, and he said: ""There is no truth in it, its chain of narrators is Shahr bin Hushab, and the narrator named Shahr is weak, and there is doubt about the 'marfu' of this hadith."" The narrator becomes anxious in reciting the hadith."
"363","Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" This hadith is ""transmitted"", and this hadith is ""continuously"" transmitted from the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah, but it is not authentic. The narrator of this hadith is Abu Bakr bin Maryam."
"364","Rashid bin Saad narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"365","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"366","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Both ears are part of the head."" A narrator of this tradition, Abd Hakim, is not considered authentic."
"367","``Urwa bin Qubaysa, on the authority of an Ansari, quoted the saying of Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father: \You people know this! The two ears are part of the head.\"""""""
"368","Narrated Umrah: I asked Sayyida Aisha about the two ears, and she replied: \These two ears are part of the head.\"" Then he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the outer and inner parts of both ears while performing ablution. One of the narrators of this tradition is Yaman \""weak\""."""""
"369","Abd Khair narrates: Once Sayyiduna Ali (RA) came and sat in the courtyard after offering the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: ""Bring me water for ablution!"" The servant brought water to you in a vessel, he brought a saucer with him, we were looking at Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both palms, then he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both his hands, he did this three times. A narrator named Abd Khair narrates: Every time he washed his hands, he did not put his hand in the vessel, until he washed both hands three times, then he put his right hand in the vessel and rinsed (by taking water through it), poured water into his nose, wiped his nose with his left hand, he did this three times, then he washed his right arm three times up to the elbow, then he put his left hand in the vessel and filled it with water, then As much water as was in it, he raised his hand with that water and wiped it with his left hand and then he wiped his head once with both his hands. Then he poured water on his left foot three times with his right hand and washed it three times with his left foot. Whoever likes to see the way of ablution of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then this is his way.” Some narrators have reduced or increased some of his words, but their meaning is close."
"370","Ayyub bin Abdullah narrates: I saw Hasan bin Abul Hasan, he asked for water for ablution, and a large pot of water was brought to him, then the water was poured into the bowl, he first washed both hands three times, then rinsed them three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head, then wiped both ears. And trimmed his beard, then washed both his feet up to the ankles, then narrated this: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu narrated this hadith to me."
"371","Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution. He (PBUH) wiped the front and back of his head and both ears, then he (PBUH) inserted his index fingers and wiped the outside and inside of the ear with them."
"372","Hameed narrates: Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to wipe the top and inside of his ears when performing ablution, and then he would say: ""I saw the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, do this."" Other narrators have narrated it on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) as his act."
"373","Hameed narrates: I saw Sayyidna Anas bin Malik performing ablution, he wiped the inside and outside of both his ears and then said: \Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud used to order (to wipe both ears).\"""""""
"374","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would gently touch both his cheeks and then use his fingers to stroke his beard from below."
"375","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform ablution (after that he narrated it according to the previous hadith). However, he did not quote this hadith as a \marfu'\"" hadith and that is correct."""""
"376","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that: When he used to wipe his head, he would lift his cap and wipe the front part of his head."
"377","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed me: \When we perform ablution for prayer"
"378","Abu Ammar narrates: He has had the privilege of visiting some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (He then narrated the entire incident). Sayyiduna Amr bin Absa (RA) narrated: ""I said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something about ablution!"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution, he should first rinse, then put water in his nose and clean his nose, then all his sins, even from the bamboo of his nose, all the sins come out with the water. Then when he washes his face, as Allah commanded him, all the sins from his face, even from the edges of his beard, fall with the water. Then when he washes both his arms up to the elbows, all the sins of his arms, even the nails, fall with the water. fall down, then he gets up and praises Allah according to His glory, praises Him, then offers two rak'ahs of prayer, then he is (purified) from his sins, as it was on the day when his mother gave birth to him."""
"379","This tradition is narrated along with another document. Its certificate is \proven\"" and \""authentic\""."""""
"380","Abd al-Rahman bin Sabat narrated this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA), or perhaps on the authority of the brother of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA): Once the Prophet (PBUH) saw some people (doing ablution), the water of one of them had not reached the heel of a dirham, or perhaps the size of a nail, so the Prophet (PBUH) began to say: It's a waste.\ (The narrator narrates:) \""A man should examine this"
"381","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once a person came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he had performed ablution and left a part of his foot as much as a nail (the water did not reach there), so the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Go back and perform ablution well.\"" A narrator named Jarir bin Hazim is unique in narrating this tradition from Qatadah and this narrator is reliable."""""
"382","Salim, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, has quoted the statement of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, on the authority of Sayyiduna Omar, who said: ""Once I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while a man came."" This is narrated in another hadith, Salem has narrated this tradition from Sayyidna Abu Bakr Radi Allahu Anhu and Sayyidna Umar Radi Allahu Anhu with reference to Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar RA. The narrator narrates: Once a person came, who had performed ablution and he did not reach the part of the back of his foot, which was the size of the big toe of his foot (i.e. that part was left dry during ablution), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go back and complete your ablution!"" So the man did just that."
"383","The meaning of this hadith is close to each other, one of its narrators, Waza' bin Nafi', has been described as weak in the knowledge of hadith."
"384","Ubaid bin Umayr narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab once saw a person whose feet were partially dry and while performing ablution, water did not reach there. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered him: \Let him wash this dry place and pray again.\"""""""
"385","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA): Once he saw a person whose back part of his feet was dry, the water did not reach there, then Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to him: ""Have you joined the prayer with this ablution?"" He said: ""O Commander of the Faithful! It is very cold and I have nothing to stop it."" Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, had started to be harsh with him before, but after hearing this, he softened and said to him: ""Wash the part of your foot that you have left, and pray again."" Then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) instructed him to fight."
"386","Alaa bin Ziyad narrates the following on the authority of one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Once, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. You had bathed, but part of your body was left dry where the water did not reach. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This part has remained dry, water has not reached here?"" The blessed Prophet's hair was thick, he moistened that part with the moisture of his (wet) hair. One of the narrators of this hadith is Abd Salam bin Salih visual and not authentic. Other reliable narrators have narrated it as a ""Mursal"" tradition, via a narrator named Ishaq, via a narrator named Alaa."
"387","Alaa bin Ziyad narrated: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a little dry spot on his neck. This tradition is transmitted and it is correct."
"388","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a special cloth with which he used to dry his limbs during ablution. The narrator of this tradition is Abu Mu'adh, Sulaiman bin Arqam and it is obsolete."
"389","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, I took the water left over from his ablution and poured it into my well."
"390","Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father, Sayyidna Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the first revelation was revealed to him, Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and showed him how to perform ablution and pray. When he finished his ablution, he took water in a chloe and sprinkled it on his private parts."
"391","Sayyiduna Osama Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When Sayyidna Jibraeel (peace be upon him) was revealed to the Prophet (peace be upon him) (in the early days), he showed the Prophet (peace be upon him) how to perform ablution."
"392","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: \Ghusl becomes wajib when the private part meets the private part.\"" When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this"
"393","It was narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA): She was asked about a person who has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate, then Sayida Aisha (RA) said: ""When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this, we both used to take ghusl together."" This same tradition is transmitted as a ""marfu'"" tradition in some other contexts, and it is transmitted as a ""suspended"" tradition with respect to some isnads."
"394","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Umm Kulthum (may God be pleased with him) narrated to me on the authority of Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with him), a person asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about a man who has intercourse with his wife and then (ends intercourse) before ejaculation, ""Would it be necessary to perform ghusl on him?"" So at that time, Sayyida Aisha (RA) was also sitting there, and the Holy Prophet (SAW) said: ""She and I (that is, Sayya A'isha (RA) sometimes do it like this, but then we take bath."")"
"395","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) offered the morning prayer. You had performed Ghusl Janabat, a verma-sized part of your blessed body was left dry where the water did not reach. It was reported: ""O Messenger of Allah! The water did not reach this place."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dripped the water from his hair on that spot and turned his hand there, he did not perform the prayer again. The narrator of this hadeeth is Mutawakkil Bin Fazeel Zaeef. This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, one of the narrators of which is a Mutrook Hadith."
"396","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a small area on his skin where the water had not reached, so he squeezed some water from his hair and applied that water to that place."
"397","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person has intercourse with a woman, ghusl becomes obligatory on him, whether he has ejaculated or not."""
"398","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a man has intercourse with a woman, ghusl becomes obligatory on him."" A narrator quotes these words: ""Even if he has not ejaculated."""
"399","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ghusl becomes necessary for four reasons: because of Janabat, on Fridays, after applying the ointment, and after giving Ghusl to the dead."" One of the narrators of this hadith, Musab bin Shiba, is not authentic and neither is Hafiz."
"400","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Janabat does not affect water, it does not affect land, and it does not affect clothes (i.e., if a person who is Janabi puts his hand in water or lies down on the ground or wears any cloth, he is not impure."")"
"401","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) states: ""There is no janabat in four things: in man, in water, in earth and in clothes."""
"402","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform Ghusl Janabat, first of all he would wash both his hands, then he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, then he would insert his hand into the blessed vessel and then run the water through the roots of his hair, until when he felt that he had washed his skin thoroughly, he would fill both hands with water three times. He used to pour it on his head, then wash the whole body afterwards."
"403","Jami bin Umayr narrates: Once I attended Sayyida Aisha's service with my mother and aunt, and Sayyida Aisha said: ""The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, then he would pour water on our heads three times, and we (women) would pour water on our heads five times, because our hair was tied."""
"404","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimunah (RA) told me this, once when the Prophet (PBUH) began to perform Ghusl Janabat, I came close to him, then he washed both his hands two or maybe three times. What, then performed ablution like the ablution of prayer, then you washed your whole body with water in both palms, then you moved away from that place a little and you washed both your feet, then I brought a handkerchief to you (so that you could wipe your body) so you did not accept it."
"405","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of his aunt Sayyida Maimunah (RA), she says: ""I kept water for the bath of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), because he (PBUH) had to perform Ghusl Janabat."" He poured water on his left hand through his right hand and then washed both his hands three times, then he put his right hand into the vessel and poured water on his private parts, then he touched his hand on the wall or the ground, then he rinsed, poured water into his nose, then he washed his face and arms and then he poured water over his whole body, then he The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left that place and washed both feet."
"406","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: ""My hair used to be tightly tied in the form of braids. I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: This is enough for you. You fill your head three times with both hands and pour water. (The narrator has doubts about the wording of the hadith here) If you pour water over your entire body, then you will be purified."""
"407","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the Ghusl of Janabat."
"408","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"409","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) made it obligatory for a Janabi person to perform ablution three times and pour water into the nose. Imam Darqutni states: This hadith is invalid. No one narrated it except a narrator named Barqa, and this narrator named Barqa used to make hadiths on his own. The correct tradition is the one narrated by a narrator named Waqiyyah, which we have previously quoted as a “Mursal” tradition on the authority of Ibn Sirin: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat."
"410","Ibn Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat."
"411","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) narrates: ""If a person washes his face during Ghusl Janabat (and forgets to put water in his nose), then he will wash his nose again and put water in his nose and pray from where he left off."" Ibn 'Arafah states: ""If a man forgets to perform ablution in Ghusl Janabat and pour water into his nose, and (he remembers during the prayer), he will leave the prayer, perform ablution, pour water into his nose, and pray afresh."" Imam Darqutni states: This is the only hadith transmitted by a female narrator named Aisha bint Ajard, and the hadith transmitted by her cannot be considered authentic."
"412","Aisha bint Ajard narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will perform the prayer again in the case of forgetting to perform ablution in Janabat and putting water in the nose"
"413","Aisha bint Ajard has narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will repeat the prayer only when he is on his side.\"""""""
"414","Aisha bint Ajard narrated this about a Janbi person: \Whoever (while taking bath) forgets to rinse and put water in his nose.\"" That woman narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: \""He will rinse"
"415","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed us to rinse and pour water into the nose. This tradition is also transmitted along with another chain of transmission and it is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition. However"
"416","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, but there is some difference in its chain of transmission. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (R.A.) is not mentioned in one chain of transmission."
"417","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this: ""A man should bathe with the water left over from a woman's bath, or a woman should bathe with the water left over from a man's (bath), but both of them can bathe together."" A narrator named Shuba has narrated the opposite tradition."
"418","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Sarjis Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: ""A woman can perform ablution or ghusl with the water left over from a man's bath or ablution, but a man cannot perform ablution through the water left over from a woman's bath or ablution."" This hadith is more authentic in terms of ""mafuk"" and it is more correct."
"419","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Menstruating women and menstruating women should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""""
"420","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"421","The same hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has been narrated along with another chain of transmission and it has also been followed."
"422","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"423","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \A foreigner should not read the Qur'an at all.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""""
"424","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \A pregnant person and a menstruating woman should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""""
"425","Abu Zarif Hamdani narrates: Once we were with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) in an open field, Sayyidna Ali (RA) went to the edge of this field. By Allah! I don't know, did they urinate or defecate, they called for a vessel of water, then they washed both their hands and then joined them both and recited the first part of the Qur'an and then said: ""You can recite the Qur'an until a person is afflicted with Janabat, if he is afflicted with Janabat, then he cannot recite a single word of it."" This hadith has been authentically narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"426","According to a hadith, it was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). According to the second chain of transmission, this is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrates: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: ""O Ali! I am pleased with you with what I am pleased with myself, and I dislike for you with what I dislike with myself. Do not recite the Qur'an when you are in the state of Janabat, nor do it when you are in the state of Ruku, nor do it when you are Be in a state of prostration, and do not pray while your hair is tied, and do not bow down (in the state of bowing during the prayer) as a donkey bows its head."""
"427","Sayyiduna Abdullah Ghafqi narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate something and then he said: ""Tonic the veil for me so that I may take a bath!"" I inquired of you: ""Are you in a state of janabat?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes!"" Later, I told Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) about this, so he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: ""He has told that, the Prophet (PBUH) ate and drank something in the state of Janabat."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Yes! When I perform ablution, I can eat and drink, but I cannot recite Qur'aat until I perform ablution."""
"428","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Malik Ghafqi narrates: He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this from Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: ""When I perform ablution in the state of Janabat, I can eat and drink, but I do not offer prayers or recite the Qur'an until I have performed ghusl."""
"429","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was nothing that prevented the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from reciting the Qur’an, except when he was in a state of janabat. A narrator named Sufyan narrates: Shu'ba said to me: \I have not narrated a better hadith than him.\"""""""
"430","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"" The evidence of this tradition is excellent. Some other narrators did not mention Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas in his chain of transmission."""""
"431","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has prohibited us from saying: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""""
"432","Ikramah narrates: Once Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha was sleeping by the side of his wife, he got up and went to his maidservant who was at the edge of the house and started having intercourse with her. His wife was frightened in a dream. When she went out, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (RA) had finished with the company and was coming back. He was confronted by his wife who was holding a knife, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha (RA) said: ""What happened?"" So his wife replied: ""What is the matter, if I had found you in the state in which I saw you before, I would have put this knife between your two shoulders."" Ibn Rawaha inquired: ""Where did you see me?"" So the wife replied: ""I have seen you consorting with maidens."" So Ibn Rawaha said: ""You did not see me."" Then Sayyiduna Ibn Rawaha said: ""The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade anyone from reciting the Qur'an in the state of Janabat."" So the wife said: ""Then you recite."" So Sayyiduna Ibn Rawahha recited these verses: ""There came to us the Messenger of Allah reciting His Book, which is more famous and brighter than the bright and bright morning, He brought us guidance, after our hearts had become blind, it was guidance that was reassuring and what he said came to pass. He used to spend the night in such a position that his side was separated from the bed, when the bed of the polytheists was their weight."" were burdened by So the woman said: ""I believe in Allah and deny what I have seen with my eyes."" Then the next day, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawaha (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about this, and the Prophet (PBUH) smiled. Narrator narrates: Until I saw your side teeth."
"433","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah entered the house (after that he narrated the entire incident, in which these words are:) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah narrated that: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""""
"434","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu states: ""A menstruating woman, a pregnant woman and a postpartum woman will not recite the Qur'an."" The narrator of this tradition is Yahya, this is Ibn Abi Anisa and it is weak."
"435","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrates this statement of his father: The letter that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, also contained the following: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are ablution.\"" This hadith is \""Mussal\"" and its narrator is \""Thiqa\""."""""
"436","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates: The letter that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm (RA), when he sent him to Najran, contained the following:"
"437","Salim narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""""
"438","Abdullah ibn Abu Bakr and Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr narrate this on the authority of their father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter to him, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""""
"439","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wrote this letter to the people of Yemen, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""""
"440","Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are in the state of ablution.\"""""""
"441","Narrated Anas bin Malik: Sayyidna Umar came out with a sword hanging around his neck and was told: ""Your brother-in-law and your sister have become ungodly (i.e. they have accepted Islam)."" So Sayyiduna Umar (R.A.) came to them both, and there was an emigrant person sitting next to them, whose name was Habab. These people were reciting Surah Al-Fatiha, then Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: ""Give me this book that you have, so that I may read it."" Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wanted to read this book, but his sister told him: ""You are impure, only the pure can touch it, and bathe it or perform ablution."" So Sayyiduna Umar rose up, he performed ablution, then he took this writing and recited Surah Fatiha. The narrator of this tradition, Qasim bin Uthman, is not authentic."
"442","Alqamah narrates: Once we were on a journey with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him. So Sayyiduna Salman Farsi Radiyallahu Anhu said: ""You ask me, I have not touched the Qur'an."" Then they recited before us the verse that we wanted and at that time there was no water between us and them. All the narrators of this hadeeth are authentic and one party has disagreed with it."
"443","Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were with Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, and when he came, I said: ""O Abu Abdullah! It would be appropriate if you perform ablution, so that we may inquire of you about some verses."" So Sayyiduna Salman Farsi Radiyallahu Anhu said: ""I am not touching the Qur'an, it can only be touched by ablution people."" (The narrator narrates:) Then Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA) recited to us the verses that we wanted. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
"444","Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were traveling with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, then when he came, I said: ""O Abu Abdullah! Perform ablution so that we may inquire from you about some verses of the Qur'an."" So he said: ""You ask me, I am not touching it, it can only be touched by ablution people."" Then we asked Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, and he recited some verses to us before performing ablution. The text of this hadith is close, and all the evidence is authentically transmitted."
"445","This tradition along with some other isnads is narrated on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid about Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"446","Regarding Alqamah and Aswad, it has been narrated about Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He recited a verse of the Qur'an while he was performing ablution. All these credentials are authentic."
"447","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about semen on clothes, and he said: \It is like mucus and saliva. That will be enough for you. Clean it with a piece of cloth or grass.\"" Only the narrator Ishaq has narrated this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" tradition."""""
"448","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about semen on clothes: He said: \It is like phlegm and saliva"
"449","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I used to scrape semen from the clothes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it was dry, and if it was wet, I would wash it off."
"450","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: If I saw a stain (of semen) on the clothes of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to wash them. This tradition is authentic."
"451","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When semen got on the Prophet's clothes, he would wash them and go to pray, while she used to see the traces of washing on his clothes."
"452","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to think: ""Clothes do not have Janabat, the land does not have Janabat, and no one does not give Janabat to another person."" This tradition is not proven, the narrator of this tradition, a woman named Umm Qalus, is not recognized as authentic."
"453","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Janabat and he intended to sleep, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, but if he intended to eat something in that state, he would wash both his palms and eat. This tradition is authentic."
"454","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of janabat, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something (in the state of janabat), he would wash both hands and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
"455","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of Janabat, he would perform ablution before going to sleep, like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something while he was in the state of Janabat, he would wash both his hands and rinse them and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
"456","Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) narrated to me: ""Some people say: Ghusl is required due to ejaculation (although in reality) it was a leave given by the Prophet (PBUH) in the early days of Islam, after which he (PBUH) ordered us to bathe."" This tradition is authentic."
"457","Al-Zuhri narrates: I asked Urwa about a man who has intercourse, but does not ejaculate, and Urwa replied: ""The opinion of the people is this, they adopt the last commandment of the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him."" Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) told me: ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same thing and not perform ghusl, but this was before the conquest of Makkah. After that, he started performing ghusl and instructed people to perform ghusl (in such a situation)."""
"458","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to me. I was drawing water from a bucket by the side of a well at that time. He said: ""O Ammar! What are you doing?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed to you! I want to wash off the phlegm on my clothes."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Ammar! Clothes are washed for five reasons: feces, urine, vomit, blood or semen. O Ammar! Your phlegm, your tears and the water in your bladder are the same."" This hadith has only been narrated by Thabit ibn Hamad and it is very weak. The two narrators of this tradition, Ibrahim and Thabit, are weak."
"459","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of urine, because the punishment in the grave is usually due to it."" This tradition is more secure as being ""transcendent""."
"460","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no harm in the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"" The narrator of this tradition is weak."""""
"461","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""There is nothing wrong with the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten."" This tradition is not authentically proven. Some of its narrators are weak and one narrator is obsolete. According to a saying, this thing was narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""There is nothing wrong with the fat of the animal whose meat is eaten."""
"462","Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is nothing wrong with the fat of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"""""""
"463","Abdullah bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father: \There is no harm in the sight of the animal whose flesh is eaten.\"""""""
"464","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of urine, because the punishment in the grave is usually due to it."" More accurately, tradition is ""transmitted""."
"465","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Often the punishment of the grave is due to urine.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"466","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this as a ""Marfu'"" tradition: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The punishment of the grave is due to urine, so you people should avoid urine."" There is no problem in the authenticity of this tradition."
"467","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) urinated on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I picked him up hard. In one hadith are the words: He said: \Leave it alone! For it does not eat"
"468","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about the urine of a milk-drinking child: ""Water should be poured over the child's urine, and the girl's urine should be washed."" A narrator named Qatadah has made this clear: ""It is until the two of them do not eat, if they start eating, both of them will be washed."""
"469","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Water will be sprinkled on the urine of a boy and the urine of a girl will be washed.\"""""""
"470","Narrated Qatadah: ""It is when they are not eating, if they start eating, the urine of both of them will be washed away."""
"471","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the urine of a minor child got on the blessed body of the Prophet (PBUH) or on his skin, he sprinkled water on the place where the urine had got on."
"472","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says this about the child's urine: \Water should be sprinkled on the part on which it is applied.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) did the same thing when Imam Hussain bin Ali (RA) got urine. The narrator of this tradition is Ibrahim"
"473","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to come to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and go to sleep. This tradition is authentic."
"474","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates: I saw the Companions of the Holy Prophet (SAW) who used to get up to pray, and sometimes I even heard one of them snoring, but they would get up and pray again and not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mubarak has stated this: ""For us, this order is when these people used to sleep while sitting."" This hadith is authentic."
"475","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) used to wait for the call to prayer until Isha, until their heads were bowed down (i.e. they fell asleep), then they would get up and perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. This tradition is authentically transmitted."
"476","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Some people from the ``Arina tribe came to Madinah to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The climate there did not suit them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""If you people want, go to the charity camels and drink their milk and urine there."" They did so and they recovered, then they went to the herdsman of those camels and killed him and took the camels of the Prophet with them and left Islam and became apostates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent people after him. When they were caught, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off their hands and feet and put stitches in their eyes and then threw them on the rocky ground until they died in that state."
"477","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once a villager came, he urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the place be dug up, and then a bucket of water be poured over it. The villager said: ""O Messenger of Allah! A person loves some people, although he does not act like their actions."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He will be with whomever he loves."" A narrator of this tradition is Samaan Majhool."
"478","Sayyiduna Abdullah narrates: Once a villager attended the Prophet's service, he was an old man, he said: ""O Sayyidna Muhammad! When will the Hour come?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What have you prepared for this?"" He replied: ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, I have not prepared for him any more prayers or fasts, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will be with the one you love."" The narrator narrates: Then that old man went and wanted to urinate in the mosque, some people passed by him and stopped him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let him do it! Maybe, it will be Paradise."" Then they poured water on his urine."
"479","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Muaqal (RA) narrates: Once a villager stood on the edge of the mosque, he removed his apron and urinated there, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Take out the dirt from the place where he urinated and throw water on that place.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Muaqal al-Tabi and this hadith is \""Mursal\""."""""
"480","Sayyidna Safwan bin Asal narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: ""There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission for a traveler to wipe his socks for three days. However, the order of Janabat is different (so this order is only about) defecating, urinating or defecating (i.e. after that a person can wipe his socks during ablution)."" There is only one tradition in which there is a command to expel the wind."
"481","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who sees tari but does not remember Ihtlam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who remembers this. Sayyidah Umm Salim Radiyallahu Anha said: \If a woman sees this thing? Will this ruling be required for her as well?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Yes! Women are the aspect of men.\"""""""
"482","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) saying: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Ghusl is required in five cases: after Janabat, Ghusl on Friday, after bathing the dead, after bathing in the water of Hammam."" The narrator of this hadith is Musab bin Shuba, weak."
"483","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: Once he was sitting with the Prophet (PBUH), while a man came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about such a person? Who approaches a woman who is not lawful for him and what men do to women, he does to her everything, but he does not have intercourse with her."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution well, then get up and pray."" The narrator narrates: So Allah revealed this verse: ""Establish prayer in both parts of the day and also in part of the night."" Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) inquired: ""Is this ruling specific to this person or is it specific to all Muslims?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is common to all Muslims."" This tradition is authentic."
"484","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: \A prayer will not be repeated because of kissing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. In the proof of this tradition"
"485","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet of Allah used to kiss me, then he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) would go to pray and not perform ablution again."
"486","This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions, in one of which there are these words: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss while fasting. Imam Malik has quoted this saying of Imam Zuhri: ""After kissing, ablution becomes obligatory."" So if the hadith narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) regarding Zuhri is accepted as correct, then Zuhri should not have issued a fatwa against him, Allah knows best!"
"487","Imam Malik narrates this statement of Ibn Shihab Zuhri, who says: ""If a husband kisses his wife, it is obligatory to perform ablution on her."""
"488","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah used to kiss one of his wives, then he (may God bless him and grant him peace) would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. (After narrating this) Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while he was fasting."
"489","It has been narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa: She came to know a saying of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, that ablution is necessary after kissing, so Sayida Aisha said: ""The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss while fasting, and he did not perform ablution again."""
"490","There are these words in a hadith: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"""""""
"491","Urwa bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A gentleman has narrated this: Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) was asked about a person who kisses his wife after performing ablution, so Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her) said: ""The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss one of his wives and not perform ablution again."" He says: I said to Sayyida Aisha: ""If that is the case, then that wife will be you."" The narrator narrates: So Sayyida Aisha remained silent."
"492","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me and then pray and not perform ablution again. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ghalib ibn Ubaidullah, and it is obsolete."
"493","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and then pray and not perform ablution again."
"494","Ata states: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is correct."""""
"495","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then go to pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Urwa narrates: I said to Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may God be pleased with her: \Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then pray and not perform ablution again. (The narrator says:) So I said: \""Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""""
"496","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast and perform ablution before praying, then if any of his wives came in front of him, he would kiss her and then perform the prayer (i.e. he would not perform ablution again). Narrated Urwa: I said to him: \Who else can she be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""""
"497","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, then kiss his wife, and then pray and would not perform ablution again. Both of them have the same word."
"498","This tradition is also narrated along with another document. Sufyan Al-Thawri, who has the most knowledge about this, says: The narrator named Habib has not heard hadiths from Urwa."
"499","Narrated ``Urwah: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) used to pray, even though drops of blood were falling on the mat. Similarly, with regard to kissing, the narrator named Yahya has described: \Describe it from me.\"" The status of both of them is the same"
"500","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution and after performing ablution he would kiss (his wife) and then pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Waqiyyah has stated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mahdi has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her (his wife) and not perform ablution again. Narrated Abu Asim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) and then pray and not perform ablution again. The same hadith has been narrated along with some other traditions, but there is some difference in its traditions. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and not perform ablution again, Allah knows best!"
"501","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and would not perform ablution again. (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) You used to pray."
"502","It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and then pray."
"503","Ms. Sayyida Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to perform ablution for prayer and then kiss (his wife) and not perform ablution again."
"504","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss her while he was fasting. Uthman bin Abu Sha'ba has narrated in the same way."
"505","Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of Sayyidah Zaynab: He asked Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) about a person who kisses his wife and touches her. So Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) replied: \Sometimes the Prophet (PBUH) would perform ablution and then kiss me and then go back and pray and would not perform ablution again.\"" The narrator of this tradition is an anonymous narrator named Zainab and such a tradition cannot be presented as evidence."""""
"506","Amr Ibn Shuaib narrates this on the authority of Sayyidah Zaynab: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) used to kiss her and then pray and not perform ablution again. According to Ata, kissing does not require ablution."
"507","This tradition is also narrated along with another document."
"508","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss one of his wives and then not perform ablution again. Here the narrator's statement that this hadith is narrated from Abdullah bin Ghalib is an illusion. What they meant was: It was narrated from Ghalib bin Ubaidullah, and this narrator is obsolete."
"509","Ata is convinced: \Kissing does not require ablution.\"""""""
"510","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) while he was fasting, then after that he would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. It is flawed in several respects."
"511","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): According to him, kissing does not make ablution necessary."
"512","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"513","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with him), she says: Once at night I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the bed. I am, only You can be helped in Your presence and I cannot praise You and I cannot describe Your praise, Your praise is the same as You yourself have described Your own praise. There are some differences in the authenticity of this tradition."
"514","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat (in the cold season) and I had not yet done Ghusl Janabat."
"515","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on my bed, so I got up. I thought that he had gone to visit his maidservant Maria. They were praying in the state of: ""O Allah! I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure, and I seek Your refuge in Your presence. I cannot express Your praise, so it is as if You yourself have expressed Your praise."" One of the narrators of this tradition is Faraj bin Fazala, weak. Some other narrators have disagreed with its transmission and narrate this tradition as a ""Mursal"" hadith."
"516","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: ""Whoever kisses his wife while she is in a state of ablution, then he should perform ablution again."" This tradition is authentic."
"517","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \Kissing is part of touching (which is mentioned in the Qur'an)"
"518","Salim narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): He said this about a man kissing and touching his wife with his hand: ""This is part of malamast, so if a person kisses his wife and touches her with his hand, ablution becomes obligatory on him."" This tradition is authentic."
"519","Salim narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He used to think: ""Kissing is part of Lams (touching, which is mentioned in the Qur'an)."" And Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered to perform ablution in this regard."
"520","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said this about kissing: \It makes ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"521","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: \Kissing is a part of 'touching'.\"""""""
"522","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"523","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of touch and it becomes necessary to perform ablution on it.\"" Ibn 'Arafah and the narrator Ma'ali have added this: \""Touch is something other than intercourse.\"" And this is authentic."""""
"524","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""""
"525","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""""
"526","The same hadith has been narrated in the same way along with some other traditions."
"527","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: ""When a person touches his private parts, he should not pray until he performs ablution."" The narrator narrates: Urwa denied this, so he inquired from Basra about it, and Basra confirmed what he had said. This is authentic. Some other narrators have adapted it, in which it is also mentioned: Arwa says: ""I asked Basra about this: so he confirmed it."""
"528","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution like the ablution of prayer.\"" This tradition is authentic."""""
"529","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: \When a person touches his private parts"
"530","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution again.\"""""""
"531","Nafi', narrates the saying of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Whoever touches his private parts, he should perform ablution like the ablution of prayer."""
"532","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""When a person moves his hand towards his private area, even if there is no hijab (cloth) between his hand and his private area, then that person performs ablution like the ablution of prayer (i.e. it becomes necessary to perform ablution on him)."""
"533","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: ""When a man touches his private parts, he should perform ablution, and when a woman touches her private parts, she should perform ablution."""
"534","Amr bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: ""Whoever touches his private parts, he should perform ablution, and whoever touches her private parts, he should perform ablution."""
"535","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is ruin for those who touch their private parts and offer prayers without performing ablution."" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""May my parents be sacrificed to you! This ruling is for men, what is your opinion about women?"" So the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""When a woman touches her private parts, she should perform ablution for prayer."" The pure narrator of this tradition is Abd al-Rahman Umari, weak."
"536","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever touches his private parts or touches his testicles and touches his pubic area should perform ablution."" This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions, however, the narrator is delusional in mentioning the testicles and the smelly place, because this thing is not mentioned in the tradition narrated from Sayyidah Basrah. More secure is this: This is the saying of Arwa and it is transmitted as a ""marfu'"" hadith, the authentic narrators have narrated it in the same way."
"537","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: ""Whoever touches his private parts, he should perform ablution."" The narrators narrate: Arwah narrates: ""Whoever touches his genital area or his testicles or touches his private parts should perform ablution."" These words are narrated by a narrator named Abu Ash-Sha'at, and this tradition is ""authentic""."
"538","Hisham bin Arwah narrates: My father used to say: ""When a person touches his private parts or his testicles or his private parts, he should not pray until he performs ablution."" All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
"539","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the honor of being the companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person touches his private parts or his testicles"
"540","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this statement of his father: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). At that time, people were busy building the mosque of Medina. Narrator narrates: People were moving stones at that time. The narrator narrates: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall I not do the same as these people are moving (stones)?"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No! Rather, you turn them into slurry, O people of Yamama!, because you are expert in this."" The narrator narrates: I made them and they began to carry them away."
"541","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement from his father: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he asked him about touching the private parts. A narrator named Ibn Abi Hatim narrates: I asked my father (Abu Hatim) and Sayyiduna Abu Shaykh Zarrah Razi about this tradition narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Jabir, and they both replied: \The narrator named Qays bin Talaq is not one to be accepted as authentic.\"" So these two gentlemen showed this narrator to be weak and did not declare him as authentic."""""
"542","Abu Uthman Nahdi narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) narrated this. It is narrated in a hadith: A narrator named Asma bin Malik Hatami, who was a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated this: A person said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I got an itch during the prayer. When I itched, my hand touched my private part."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Sometimes) I also do this."""
"543","Qays bin Talaq narrates the statement of his father Sayyiduna Talq bin Ali (RA): We set out in a delegation to attend the presence of the Prophet (PBUH), when we entered his presence, we pledged allegiance to him and prayed in his lead. Have an opinion?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \He is a piece of your body.\"" (The narrator doubts"
"544","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this on the authority of his father: We asked the Prophet (PBUH) about touching the private parts, and he (PBUH) said: “It is a part of your body.” The narrator of this tradition is Ayyub, unknown."
"545","A Muhaddith named Raja bin Marji narrates: Once we gathered in the mosque of Khaif, among whom were Ahmad bin Hanbal, Ali bin Madini and Yahya bin Mu'in, and a discussion broke out between them about touching the private parts, and Yahya said: ""After this, ablution will be performed."" Ali bin Madini expressed his opinion according to the opinion of the people of Kufa and imitated their opinion. Yahya bin Mu'in quoted the hadith of Basrah bint Safwan in support of his position, while Ali bin Madini quoted the hadith of Qays bin Talq in support of his position. He said to Yahya: ""How can you follow the authority of Basra? While Marwan (who was the governor of Madinah), he sent a soldier, until that soldier came to Marwan with the woman's answer."" So Yahya said: ""Many people have criticized Qays bin Talaq and have not declared his tradition to be authentic."" So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said: ""What you both described, the incident is like this."" Yahya al-Mahdi, on the authority of Imam Malik, narrates the following about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, says: ""It is not necessary to perform ablution after this, it is a part of your body."" So Yahya inquired: ""Who has copied this?"" So he replied: ""This is what Sufyan narrated on the authority of Abu Qais on the authority of Hazeel, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him)."" So whenever the opinions of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masood (RA) and Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) differ on a matter, then Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masood is more deserving of being followed. So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said to them, ""It is so."" But the narration of the narrator Abu Qais cannot be presented as an argument. So he said: ""Abu Na'im has narrated this statement of Sayyidina Ammar bin Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Mu'mar, regarding Umayr."" He says: ""I do not care whether I touch it (the private part) or touch my nose."" So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said: ""Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) are both of the same generation, so whoever wants to adopt their opinion and whoever wants to adopt their opinion."""
"546","Shaqiq narrates: Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: \I do not care if I touch my private parts or touch my nose while I am in the state of prayer.\"""""""
"547","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \I do not care whether I touch my private part or touch my ear during prayer.\"""""""
"548","Ubaidullah narrates: Sayyiduna Umar was asked about touching the armpit, and he said: \Wudhu will be performed after that.\"""""""
"549","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""""
"550","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""""
"551","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu says: ""When a person touches his armpit, he should perform ablution."""
"552","Hammad bin Zayd has stated this: When Ayub was mentioned about touching the armpits, he said: ""Some armpits are like that, one should perform ghusl after touching them."""
"553","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Wudhu must be performed on what comes out, but what enters inside does not need to be performed."""
"554","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his back on and prayed and did not perform ablution again, he only washed the part where he put his back on. Ibn Abu Ashreen narrates this tradition as a ""marfu'"" hadith, while a narrator named Abu Mughira narrates it as ""suspended"" on the authority of Uza'i, and this is correct."
"555","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution (washing his face), he would touch his cheeks and stroke his beard downwards with his fingers."
"556","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): When he performed ablution, he would touch his two cheeks and sometimes stroke his beard with his fingers, and sometimes leave it off. This tradition is \suspended\"" and rightly so."""""
"557","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he gently touched his cheeks and stroked his beard with his fingers."
"558","Qatadah and Yazid al-Raqashi have narrated this: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
"559","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Safar narrated to us that Ibrahim bin Hani narrated to us, he said that Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, he said that Uza’i narrated to us, he said that Abdul Wahid bin Qays narrated to us, he said that Yazid al-Raqashi narrated this hadith from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if this hadith is “Mursal” (meaning the middle narrator is missing), then it is also authentic."
"560","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: ""When a person has a hemorrhage during his prayer, he should go back, wash off the blood and perform ablution again and pray anew."" The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Arqam, obsolete."
"561","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""The water of the sea is the ablution water of the angels. When they descend, they perform ablution with it, and when they ascend, they perform ablution with it."""
"562","Sayyiduna Ali bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a person passes out during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution again, and pray again."""
"563","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a person vomits or belches bitterly during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution, and start reciting more than what he had already prayed. This is when he has not said anything in between."" A narrator named Ibn Juraj has narrated this, ""If he speaks, he will pray anew."""
"564","Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""When a person vomits or belches sourly during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution, and perform his prayer from the same place (from where he left it), this is when he has not spoken."" Ibn Jaraj narrates."
"565","This hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"566","This hadith is also narrated along with another document."
"567","Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever belches or vomits or has a hemorrhage (and this happens during prayer), then he should go back, perform ablution again, and complete his prayer."""
"568","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"569","This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) along with another chain of transmission. The same tradition is also transmitted as \Mursal\"" along with another document."""""
"570","Ibn Juraj narrates this on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""When a person bleeds or vomits during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution, and return and continue the prayer from where he left it, (this ruling is until) he has finished speaking."""
"571","Ibn Jaraj has narrated a similar tradition on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikah, on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha, and on the authority of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"572","Ibn Jurayj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: ""When a person vomits during prayer, or belches sourly, or passes wind, then he should go back, perform ablution, and return and start his prayer from the place (from where he left it), this is when he has not uttered a word."" A narrator named Abu Bakr has stated this: It is correct to transmit it from Ibn Jaraj as a ""Mursal"" tradition, however, a narrator Ismail bin Ayyash has narrated it on the authority of Ibn Jarij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikah on the authority of Sayyida Aisha, there is no truth to it."
"573","Ibn Jaraj, in reference to his father, quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Whoever has a hemorrhage, vomits, or belches, then he should perform ablution and perform ablution as much as he had prayed, then complete the remaining prayer, and he should refrain from speaking to anyone."""
"574","Imam Zayd bin Ali narrates this statement of his grandfather, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ""Sour belching or (vomiting) breaks ablution."" The narrator of this tradition is Sawar, it is obsolete, and no one else has narrated this tradition with reference to Sayyiduna Zayd."
"575","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: ""When a person feels a rumbling in his stomach, vomits, or has a hemorrhage, he should go back (perform ablution) and return to pray from where he left, this is when he has not spoken to anyone."""
"576","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: ""When a person is leading the people in prayer and feels a rumbling in his stomach or he has a hemorrhage or vomits, he should put a cloth over his nose and hold the hand of one of the people present and lead him forward."""
"577","Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet saw me, blood was flowing from my nose, so he said: \Perform ablution again.\"" A narrator named Mahamali has made this clear: \""It means you perform ablution"
"578","This same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: ""His haemorrhage broke out, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should perform ablution again because of this."" The narrator of this tradition is Amr Qureshi, Amr bin Khalid, Abu Khalid Wasti, which is a lost hadith. Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and Yahya bin Mu'in have stated this: ""Abu Khalid Wasti is a liar."""
"579","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: If the Prophet (PBUH) had a haemorrhage during the prayer, he (PBUH) would perform ablution and perform the remaining prayer. The narrator of this tradition is ``Amr bin Riyah, obsolete."
"580","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed the prayer after ablution and did not perform ablution again. The Prophet (PBUH) only washed the place where he had put his heels."
"581","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: ""Wudhu becomes necessary after every bleeding."" The narrator of this tradition, Sayyidna Umar bin Abdul Aziz, did not listen to the hadiths from Tamim Dari and did not visit them, while the two narrators of this tradition, Yazid bin Khalid, Yazid bin Muhammad, are both unknown."
"582","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \It is not necessary to perform ablution if one or two drops of blood appear"
"583","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""A drop or two drops of blood does not make ablution obligatory, until the blood starts to flow (it is not obligatory until then)."" The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Fazl bin Utbah, weak, and Sufyan bin Zia and Hajjaj bin ??? are also weak."
"584","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has a hemorrhage during prayer, he should perform ablution and (perform the prayer from where he left it)."" The narrator of this tradition is Abu Bakr Dahiri, Abdullah bin Hakim, the abandoned hadith."
"585","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever breaks his ablution, if he is in the state of prayer, he should put his hand over his nose and go back, so that it is evident that his hemorrhage has broken out."""
"586","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person breaks his ablution during prayer"
"587","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: ""When a person breaks his ablution during prayer, then he should hold his nose and then go back."""
"588","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has permitted the blood of boils and abscesses (it does not require ablution)."
"589","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever breaks his ablution during prayer should hold his nose and then go back and perform ablution.\"""""""
"590","Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) ended his fast by saying this. The narrator narrates: Later, I met Sayyidna Thawban (RA) in the Jamia Masjid of Damascus, I mentioned this to him, and he said (Abu Dardaa said the truth) that I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH)."
"591","A narrator named Saad narrated: Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrated this hadith to him, then he narrated a similar hadith from the Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (RA) and on the authority of Sayyidna Thawban (RA)."
"592","Ma'dan bin Abu Talha narrates this: Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) told him, after that he mentioned the previous hadeeth, in which it is mentioned: (Sayyidna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \I performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).\"""""""
"593","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which there are these words: Sayyidna Thawban (RA) said: ""He has said the truth, I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH)."""
"594","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Whenever I perform ablution (blood) starts flowing."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution, if it continues to flow from your top to your feet, then it is not necessary to perform ablution on you."" Ramwi named Abdullah bin Malik, this is weak, this tradition is not authentic."
"595","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting. It was something other than Ramadan. He suffered something that tormented him, which caused him to vomit. Then he vomited. Then he called me for ablution and performed ablution and ended the fast. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is it obligatory to perform ablution after vomiting?"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If this was a duty, you would have received its command."" The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had fasted the next day, so I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""This is the judgment of my breaking the fast of the previous day."" This hadith has been narrated only by Atiya bin Sakin with reference to Uza'i, a person who rejects the hadith."
"596","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) fell asleep, he was in a state of prostration at that time, until he started snoring, then he stood up and prayed. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You were asleep."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Wudhu is obligatory on a person who sleeps lying down, because when he sleeps lying down, his joints become loose."" A narrator named Abu Khalid is unique in quoting this tradition with reference to Abu Qatada. This tradition is not reliable."
"597","Sayyiduna Mu'awiya bin Abu Sufyan (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The eye is the closure of the anus, so when the eye falls asleep, this closure is broken."""
"598","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"599","Sayyidna Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""Whoever sleeps while sitting, it is not necessary to perform ablution on him, but whoever puts his side (on the ground), it is necessary to perform ablution on him."""
"600","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \The eye is a blockage of the anus. Whoever sleeps"
"601","Abu Malih narrates this on the authority of his father: Once we were praying in the company of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and a man who was blind came, and we laughed when he fell into the pit, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered us to perform complete ablution again and pray anew. The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which both Hasan bin Dinar and Hasan bin Amara are weak narrators, they have made a mistake in its chain of transmission. Hasan al-Basri has narrated this tradition on the authority of Hafsa bint Salman, on the authority of Abul Aaliya. Hasan often cites the ""Messenger"" tradition with reference to the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him). Even Hasan bin Amara has related this tradition, he has narrated this with reference to Khalid with reference to Abu Walid, with reference to his father, so this is a very ugly illusion. This tradition was narrated by Khalid on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin and Abul Aaliya from the Prophet. Sufyan al-Thawri, Hamad bin Salamah and other narrators have also narrated it in the same way. A narrator named Ibn Ishaq has quoted in his tradition with difficulty regarding transmission from Hasan bin Dinar, sometimes quoting him on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Abul Malih, on the authority of his father. Qatadah has quoted this tradition from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a “Messenger” tradition with reference to Abul Aaliyah. It has been narrated on the authority of Saad bin Abu Arooba, Muammar, Abu Awanah, Saad bin Bashir, and other narrators have narrated it on the authority of them, after that we will mention the hadith of these gentlemen."
"602","Abul Malih narrates on the authority of his father: We were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while a blind man came and fell into the pit, that is, the well in the mosque, so some people behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, laughed. The narrator of this hadith is Hasan bin Dinar, the abandoned hadith. This tradition has also been narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Amr, this narrator is also an abandoned hadith, he has narrated this tradition on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abul Aaliya, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of a narrator named Salam."
"603","Narrated Anas bin Malik: A blind person fell into a well, some people behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah has narrated this: It was narrated on the authority of Anas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was leading the people in prayer, while a blind man entered the mosque, he fell into a well, some people laughed behind the Prophet (PBUH). A narrator named Ibn Mukhlid and Sayyiduna Anas (may God be pleased with him) narrated this on the authority of Abul Aaliyah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer. There was a well in the middle of the mosque. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah narrates: This hadith is rejected. Shaykh Abul Hasan says: This hadith has been narrated from a narrator named Salam by a narrator named Abd al-Rahman, this person is a muratuk who compiles hadiths. This tradition has been narrated by Dawud bin Muhibr, this person is also obsolete, who compiles hadiths, he has narrated this tradition from Ayyub's father, who is weak, he has narrated it from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Qatadah."
"604","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading us in prayer, while a blind man came, he fell into a pit and started crying. This is the correct statement of the person who narrated it as a \Mursal\"" hadith on the authority of Qatadah"
"605","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A blind man fell into a well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer. Some of those who were praying under the guidance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at this, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again."
"606","Abul Aaliyah narrates this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer, while a man fell into the well, some of the people present laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed again to perform ablution and pray."
"607","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"608","This hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abul Aliya along with another chain of transmission."
"609","This tradition is narrated from Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"610","‘Uthman narrated to us: Ibrahim narrated to us: ‘Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Mu‘tamir narrated to us from Salm—meaning Ibn Abi al-Dhiyal—from Qatadah, who said: It has reached us from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly. And this is the authentic [narration] from Qatadah; Ma‘mar, Abu ‘Awanah, Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Arubah, and Sa‘id ibn Bashir agreed upon it, narrating it from Qatadah, from Abu al-‘Aliyah, mursal. And Salm ibn Abi al-Dhiyal followed them in narrating it from Qatadah, mursal. These are five trustworthy narrators who reported it from Qatadah, from Abu al-‘Aliyah, mursal. As for Ayyub ibn Khut, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar, ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn ‘Amr ibn Jablah, and al-Hasan ibn Dinar—all of them are abandoned (matruk), and none of them is fit to be cited as evidence even if he had no opponent; how much more so when each of them is contradicted by five trustworthy companions of Qatadah? And as for the hadith of al-Hasan ibn Dinar from al-Hasan, from Abu al-Malih, from his father—it is also far from correctness, and we know of no one who followed him upon it. ‘Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated it from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, but ‘Abd al-Karim is abandoned, and his narrator is ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn al-Husayn, who is also weak. And ‘Umar ibn Qays al-Makki, known as Sindul—who is weak, his hadith rejected—narrated it from ‘Amr ibn ‘Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from ‘Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (ﷺ). As for the hadith of ‘Abd al-Karim… [text cuts off]."
"611","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a person laughs (during the prayer), he should perform ablution again and perform the prayer again."""
"612","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: ""Whoever laughs during the prayer, then he should perform ablution again and perform the prayer."" A narrator named Hasan has stated this: ""Whoever laughs, he will repeat ablution and pray."" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Sufyan, who is weak and his status in the knowledge of hadith is very bad. This tradition along with another chain of transmission is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas bin Malik."
"613","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us—and the most favorable assessment of Sufyan ibn Muhammad is that he erred in this hadith—on the authority of Ibn Wahb, if he did not deliberately fabricate it in his statement ""from al-Hasan, from Anas."" For others have narrated it from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan, as a mursal (interrupted chain) from the Prophet ﷺ. Among them: Khalid ibn Khidash al-Muhallabi, Mawhib ibn Yazid, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb. And others did not mention Anas ibn Malik in their hadith from Ibn Wahb in the chain, nor did they mention Sulayman ibn Arqam between al-Zuhri and al-Hasan, even though he was al-Zuhri's nephew. And Ibn Abi Atiq narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ. These are four opinions from al-Hasan, all of them invalid; because al-Hasan only heard this hadith from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ."
"614","Sayyiduna Hasan Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a man with weak eyesight came, (the narrator suspects) that he was blind, he fell into the well, some people laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution. The narrator narrates: I mentioned this tradition to Hafs bin Salman, so he said: \I narrated this tradition to Hasan al-Basri with reference to Hafsa (daughter of Sirin)"
"615","Abu Ali Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us (L12530), Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi (L12383) narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini (L5792) narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi (L4493) said to me: ""This hadith revolves around Abu al-Aliyah."" So I said: ""Al-Hasan has narrated it mursalan (without mentioning the Companion)."" He said: ""Hammad ibn Zayd (L2491) narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, he said: 'I narrated it to Al-Hasan, from Hafsah, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Then Ibrahim has narrated it mursalan."" Abd al-Rahman said: ""Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Hashim, he said: 'I narrated it to Ibrahim, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Al-Zuhri has narrated it mursalan."" He said: ""I read it in the book of Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Al-Hasan."""""
"616","Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to repeat the prayer and perform ablution again."
"617","Hasan narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a person came and fell into a well."
"618","Hasan al-Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a person came and fell into the well."
"619","Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to perform ablution again and perform the prayer again."
"620","Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, after that, according to the previous hadith."
"621","Zahri said: Laughing or laughing (during the prayer) does not break Wudhu. What Zahri has quoted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Hasan, if it was correct according to Zahri, he would not have issued a fatwa against it and contrary to it, Allah knows best!"
"622","Ma'bad narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a blind man came, who fell into the pit, and some people laughed, until they laughed. When he finished the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever among you laughed"
"623","Al-Mabadi Jahani narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the morning prayer, while a blind man came, near the place of the Prophet’s prayer, there was a well, on which a bucket was placed. It has been fixed, he should perform ablution (again) and perform the prayer again."
"624","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying. A man with poor eyesight came, passed by a well (pit) with a log lying on it, and fell into the pit. Some of those who were praying behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer and said: \He who laughed among you should perform ablution again and perform the prayer.\"" These words are from a narrator named Ziyad bin Ayyub."""""
"625","Ibn Sirin narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the Companions in prayer, after that the hadith was narrated as before, but he narrated these words: When that person fell into the pit, some people laughed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave this order, after that the hadith was narrated as before. This tradition is authentic, which is narrated on the authority of Khalid on the authority of Hafsa on the authority of Abul Aaliyah. A muhaddith called Hasan says: It is narrated on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abul Malih, on the authority of his father, this is a very clear mistake. The same tradition has been narrated by some other narrators on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"626","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, while a person came who had poor eyesight and fell into a pit. The people laughed at him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered: Those who laughed should perform ablution again and pray."
"627","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"628","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer, while a man came, he placed his foot on the basket, which was placed at the head of the well, and fell into the well. Then the people behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered some of those who laughed: They should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"629","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer. There was a blind person among those present, who fell into the well. Some of the companions laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered the prayer and ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"630","This same hadith is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"631","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his Companions in prayer. Meanwhile, a man with weak eyesight passed by a pit, on which something was placed, and he fell into the pit. The same tradition is narrated from another hadith."
"632","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person came who fell into the pit, and some of the people present laughed. This tradition is transmitted along with other evidences."
"633","Abul Aaliyah narrates on the authority of an Ansari: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person with poor eyesight came and fell into the pit."
"634","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution."
"635","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person came who had weak eyesight, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he fell into the pit that was in the mosque, so some people laughed."
"636","This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"637","This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"638","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"639","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in the Fajr prayer or in the evening prayer. There was a pit in the mosque. A person with poor eyesight fell into the pit and some people laughed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and asked the people the reason for laughing, and they told him the reason."
"640","Abul Aaliyah narrates: Some of those who were praying in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) laughed, so the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: The person who laughed should perform ablution and pray again."
"641","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"642","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, there was a hole in the mosque, a person who was blind came and some people laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, those who laughed should perform ablution again and perform the prayer."
"643","Ibrahim narrates: A blind man came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at that time, he slipped and fell into the pit, so the people laughed."
"644","This hadith has been narrated as a ""Mursal"" tradition with reference to Ibrahim, while in another chain of transmission, it has been chained with reference to Ibrahim, in reference to Abul Alia, while the same chain of transmission has been chained with reference to some other chain of traditions. Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who was more familiar with Abul Aaliyah and Hasan al-Basri, used to say: Do not accept the ""Mursal"" tradition narrated by Abul Aaliyah, because both of them do not care from whom they have taken it."
"645","Asim narrates: Ibn Sirin said to me: Recite the hadith you have to recite! But do not narrate any hadith to me regarding two men from Basra: Abul Aaliyah and Hasan, because these two do not care who they get their hadith from."
"646","Muhammad bin Sirin says: There are four people who authenticate everyone who narrates their hadith and they do not care from whom they have taken the hadith. Hasan Basri, Abul Aliya, Hameed bin Hilal, Dawood bin Abu Hind. This tradition is narrated by Jabir on the authority of Amish, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, he has mentioned this hadith and also mentioned its cause."
"647","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us: He who laughs during the prayer should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. Shaykh Abu Bakr Neshapuri says: This Hadith is rejected and not authentic. It is authentically narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir to the contrary."
"648","Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"649","Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"650","Sufyan narrates: Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a person who laughs during the prayer, (so he said:) He will perform the prayer again, but ablution will not be required for him."
"651","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, he will perform the prayer again, but ablution is not required on him."
"652","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If a person laughs during the prayer, he should repeat the prayer, but it is not necessary to perform ablution on him."
"653","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He was asked about laughing during the prayer, and he said: That person will perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary for him to perform ablution."
"654","A narrator named Abu Sufyan has narrated this, Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu has said this about the one who laughs during the prayer, that person should perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary to perform ablution again. This tradition is narrated from Sha'bi along with another chain of transmission."
"655","A narrator named Abu Sufyan narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: A person who laughs during prayer does not require ablution. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"656","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"657","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary (i.e. does not break ablution)."
"658","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “Laughter breaks the prayer, but it does not break the ablution.”"
"659","There is another hadith to the contrary, narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Talking (during prayer) breaks the prayer"
"660","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that, according to him, laughing during prayer does not make ablution necessary."
"661","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Smiling does not break the prayer, unless a person laughs (the prayer does not break)."" This same hadith has been transmitted as a ""marfu'"" hadith along with another chain of transmission."
"662","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, it is necessary to perform the prayer again."
"663","Hameed bin Hilal says: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) left with a delegation, in this delegation there was a blind man from the tribe of Abdul Qays. Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) was leading the prayer. Narrated Ahnaf: When I heard his voice saying that he had fallen into the well, everyone in the audience laughed except me and Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari. Sayyiduna Abu Musa completed the prayer and inquired: What happened to these people? These people said: So-and-so had fallen into the pit, so Sayyiduna Abu Musa ordered him to pray again."
"664","Hameed bin Hilal narrates: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) was teaching his companions to pray, those companions saw something that made them laugh, so Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, after finishing the prayer, said: Whoever among you laughed should perform the prayer again."
"665","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (RA): He was leading the people in prayer, and the people saw something at which some people laughed at the example of Sayyidna Abu Musa. After completing the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: \Whoever laughed among you should perform the prayer again.\"""""""
"666","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching the Asr prayer to his companions. He smiled during the prayer. Have you smiled during prayer? The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Mikael passed by me, there was dust on his wings. He smiled at me and I smiled at him. He was returning after chasing a people (of the enemy)."""
"667","Sahl bin Mu'adh narrates on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: ""The one who laughs, looks around and snaps his fingers during the prayer has the same status."""
"668","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: A person who laughs during the prayer does not need to perform ablution on him. This order was for those who were performing the prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"669","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""The entire surface of the earth has been made a place for us to pray, and its soil has been made a source of purification for us, and our ranks have been made like the ranks of the angels."""
"670","The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, which reads: \All the earth has been made for us a place of prayer and a means of purification when we cannot find water.\"""""""
"671","Umayr, who was the slave of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Once, I and Abdullah bin Yasar, who is the slave of Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, both of us attended the service of Sayyidna Abu Jaham bin Harith Ansari, and Sayyidna Abu Jaham, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was coming from the well of Jamal. Aya, he greeted you, the Prophet did not respond to the greeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approached the wall, wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) and then greeted it."
"672","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. He met a man who was coming from the front."
"673","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. A person greeted him from the front, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to the greeting, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his blessed hand on the wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he said: “Peace be upon you too.”"
"674","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was coming to the well of the camel, perhaps after defecating or urinating. I greeted you, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to my greeting, then the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hand on the blessed wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to my greeting."
"675","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Jaham (RA) about the Holy Prophet (PBUH)."
"676","Narrated by Nafi: Once, I attended the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, in connection with some work of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visiting after defecating or urinating. This person greeted him, the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not respond to him, until the person was about to leave the street, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hands on the blessed wall and wiped his face, then turned again and wiped both his arms (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to his greeting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \I did not respond to you because I was not in a state of ablution.\"""""""
"677","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: Once the Prophet (PBUH) was coming home after defecating. A man came to him near the well of Jamal, he greeted him, the Prophet did not return his greeting until he came to the wall and wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) then returned the man's greeting."
"678","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said this about Allah's commandment: ""If you are sick or on a journey."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: ""When a person gets a wound in the way of Allah, or has an abscess or scabies, then has Janabat or fears that he may die because of taking ghusl, such a person will perform Tayammum."""
"679","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \It is permissible for a sick person to perform tayammum through clay.\"""""""
"680","Ata narrated this tradition as a marfu', hadith, up to the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, while other narrators narrated it as a muwaqf tradition."
"681","Sayyiduna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Once I had a fever in a winter night, it was a matter of Ghazwa Zaat-ul-Salsil, I was afraid that if I bathed, I would be killed, so I performed Tayammum and led the morning prayer to my companions. Later, when this was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he inquired: \O Amr! Did you lead your companions in prayer while you were in Janabat?\"" So I told you about the reason that prevented me from taking bath. I said: I heard Allah saying: \""Do not kill yourselves"
"682","Abu Qais, who is the slave of Sayyidna Amr bin As, narrates: Once Sayyidna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, went to a house. During this time they had to pack for the cold, it had never been so cold before. When he started to go for the morning prayer, he said: ""By Allah! I had a cold last night. Such cold, by Allah! I have never seen it."" Then he washed his legs (where there was a sign of Ithlam), performed ablution for the prayer and led his companions in prayer. When he attended the Prophet's service, the Prophet asked his companions: ""How did you find Amr, how was his company?"" So he greatly praised Sayyiduna Amr (and also said): ""O Messenger of Allah! Once he taught us the prayer in the state of Janabat."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyidna Amr, Sayyidna Amr told him about this situation and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace! Allah said: 'Do not kill yourself.' So the Holy Prophet (PBUH) smiled at Sayyiduna Amr's words."
"683","Rabi bin Badr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyiduna Asla said: ""You show me how the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught you how to perform tayammum."" So they put their two palms together on the ground, then blew on them, then wiped their faces with them, even wiped their beards, then put both hands on the ground, wiped the ground with them, one of them joined the other. He wiped the outside and inside of his palm. In a hadith these words are: The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) taught me how to anoint? The narrator narrates: Then he placed both his palms on the ground, then raised them towards his face, then made a second stroke, then wiped the outer and inner parts of both hands until he wiped the elbows with his hands."
